/** All translations for zizhitongjian ch.009 — Garrett M. Petersen (2026), Composer 2.5 */
export const entries = [
  { zh: "__FORCETOC___", literal: "—", idiomatic: "—" },
  { zh: "起旃蒙協洽，盡柔兆涒灘，凡二年。", literal: "From Zhanmeng Xiehe through Rouzhao Tuantan; two years in all.", idiomatic: "From Zhanmeng Xiehe through Rouzhao Tuantan—two years in all." },
  { zh: "1冬，十月，沛公至霸上。", literal: "1. In winter, the tenth month, the Duke of Pei reached Bashang.", idiomatic: "1. In the tenth month of winter the Duke of Pei reached Bashang." },
  { zh: "秦王子嬰素車、白馬，系頸以組，封皇帝璽、符、節，降軹道旁。", literal: "The king of Qin, Ziying, came in an unadorned cart with a white horse, bound his neck with a cord, sealed up the emperor's seal, tallies, and batons, and surrendered beside the road at Zhi.", idiomatic: "King Ziying of Qin came in a plain cart drawn by a white horse, a cord about his neck, bearing the imperial seal, tallies, and batons, and surrendered by the road at Zhi." },
  { zh: "諸將或言誅秦王。", literal: "Some of the generals said the king of Qin should be executed.", idiomatic: "Some generals urged that the king of Qin be put to death." },
  { zh: "沛公曰：「始懷王遣我，固以能寬容。", literal: "The Duke of Pei said: \"When King Huai first sent me forth, it was precisely because I can be forbearing.", idiomatic: "The Duke of Pei said: \"King Huai sent me because I know how to show forbearance." },
  { zh: "且人已降，殺之不祥。", literal: "Moreover, the man has already surrendered; to kill him is inauspicious.", idiomatic: "And he has already surrendered—to kill him would be ill-omened." },
  { zh: "」乃以屬吏。", literal: "\" He then handed him over to the clerks.", idiomatic: "\" He handed him over to the officials instead." },
  { zh: "::賈誼論曰：秦以區區之地致萬乘之權，招八州而朝同列，百有餘年，然後以六合為家，殽、函為宮。", literal: ":: Jia Yi observes in his treatise: Qin, from a mere corner of territory, attained the authority of ten thousand chariots, summoned the eight provinces, and made its peers bow at court; after more than a hundred years it then took all within the four seas as its household and Xiao and Han as its palace.", idiomatic: ":: Jia Yi writes: From a scrap of land Qin won the power of ten thousand chariots, drew the eight provinces to court, and for a century and more made peers bow; only then did it take all within the four seas as its house and Xiao and Han as its walls." },
  { zh: "一夫作難而七廟墮，身死人手，為天下笑者，何也？", literal: "One man raised trouble and the seven temples fell; his person died in another's hands and he became the laughingstock of all under Heaven—why?", idiomatic: "One man rebelled and the seven temples crumbled; he died in another's hands and became the world's jest—why?" },
  { zh: "仁誼不施而攻守之勢異也。", literal: "Benevolence and righteousness were not extended, and the balance of attack and defense had shifted.", idiomatic: "Because benevolence and righteousness were never shown, and the balance of attack and defense had changed." },
  { zh: "沛公西入咸陽，諸將皆爭走金帛財物之府分之。", literal: "The Duke of Pei entered Xianyang from the west; the generals all raced to the treasuries of gold, silk, and goods to divide them.", idiomatic: "The Duke of Pei marched west into Xianyang. Every general raced to the vaults of gold, silk, and goods to seize a share." },
  { zh: "蕭何獨先入收秦丞相府圖籍藏之，以此沛公得具知天下□厄塞、戶口多少、強弱之處。", literal: "Xiao He alone entered first, gathered the maps and registers from the Qin chancellor's office and stored them away; by this the Duke of Pei was able to know fully all under Heaven's □ passes and barriers, how many households there were, and where strength and weakness lay.", idiomatic: "Xiao He alone went in first, gathered the maps and registers from the Qin chancellor's office, and hid them away. Thus the Duke of Pei came to know every chokepoint □ across the realm, every count of households, and where power lay strong or weak." },
  { zh: "沛公見秦宮室、帷帳、狗馬、重寶、婦女以千數，意欲留居之。", literal: "The Duke of Pei saw the Qin palaces, curtains, dogs and horses, heavy treasures, and women by the thousands, and his heart wished to remain and dwell there.", idiomatic: "The Duke of Pei saw Qin's palaces, hangings, hounds and horses, heavy treasure, and women by the thousand—and meant to stay." },
  { zh: "樊噲諫曰：「沛公欲有天下耶，將為富家翁耶？", literal: "Fan Kuai remonstrated, saying: \"Does the Duke of Pei wish to possess all under Heaven, or does he mean to become a rich household head?", idiomatic: "Fan Kuai urged him: \"Do you mean to win the realm, my lord, or only to become a rich man?\"" },
  { zh: "凡此奢麗之物，皆秦所以亡也，沛公何用焉！", literal: "All these lavish things are what brought Qin to ruin—of what use are they to the Duke of Pei!", idiomatic: "All this luxury is what destroyed Qin—what use is it to you!" },
  { zh: "願急還霸上，無留宮中！", literal: "I beg you to hurry back to Bashang and not linger in the palace!", idiomatic: "Return to Bashang at once—do not linger in the palace!\"" },
  { zh: "」沛公不聽。", literal: "\" The Duke of Pei would not heed him.", idiomatic: "\" The Duke of Pei would not listen." },
  { zh: "張良曰：「秦為無道，故沛公得至此。", literal: "Zhang Liang said: \"Qin was without the Way, and therefore the Duke of Pei was able to reach here.", idiomatic: "Zhang Liang said: \"Qin lost the Way—that is why you stand here." },
  { zh: "夫為天下除殘賊，宜縞素為資。", literal: "One who removes cruel villains for all under Heaven ought to take plain white as his standard.", idiomatic: "A man who rids the realm of tyrants should dress in mourning white." },
  { zh: "今始入秦，即安其樂，此所謂『助桀為虐』。", literal: "Now, having just entered Qin, to settle at once into its pleasures—this is what is called 'helping Jie to torment the people.'", idiomatic: "To enter Qin and at once take its ease—this is what men call 'helping Jie torment his people.'\"" },
  { zh: "且忠言逆耳利於行，毒藥苦口利於病，願沛公聽樊噲言！", literal: "Moreover, loyal words grate on the ear yet profit conduct; bitter medicine tastes harsh yet profits the illness—I beg the Duke of Pei to heed Fan Kuai's words!", idiomatic: "Loyal counsel grates on the ear yet serves the deed; bitter medicine tastes foul yet cures the sickness. Hear Fan Kuai, my lord!\"" },
  { zh: "」沛公乃還軍霸上。", literal: "\" The Duke of Pei then withdrew his army to Bashang.", idiomatic: "\" The Duke of Pei withdrew his army to Bashang." },
  { zh: "十一月，沛公悉召諸縣父老、豪桀，謂曰：「父老苦秦苛法久矣！", literal: "In the eleventh month the Duke of Pei summoned all the elders and leading men of the counties and said to them: \"You fathers and elders have long suffered under Qin's harsh laws!", idiomatic: "In the eleventh month the Duke of Pei summoned the elders and leading men of every county and said: \"You have suffered Qin's harsh laws long enough!" },
  { zh: "吾與諸侯約，先入關者王之，吾當王關中。", literal: "I made a covenant with the feudal lords that whoever entered the passes first would be king; I ought to be king in Guanzhong.", idiomatic: "I swore with the lords that whoever entered the passes first would rule them—and I entered first. I ought to be king in Guanzhong." },
  { zh: "與父老約法三章耳：殺人者死，傷人及盜抵罪。", literal: "I make with you fathers and elders only a three-article law: killers die; those who wound or steal answer to the crime.", idiomatic: "I give you only three laws: murderers die; wounders and thieves answer for their crimes." },
  { zh: "餘悉除去秦法，諸吏民皆案堵如故。", literal: "All the rest of Qin's laws I abolish entirely; every clerk and commoner shall live undisturbed as before.", idiomatic: "Every other Qin statute I abolish. Clerks and people alike shall live undisturbed as before." },
  { zh: "凡吾所以來，為父老除害，非有所侵暴，無恐。", literal: "All that I have come for is to remove harm for you fathers and elders, not to invade or oppress—do not fear.", idiomatic: "I came only to lift harm from you—not to plunder. Have no fear." },
  { zh: "且吾所以還軍霸上，待諸侯至而定約束耳。", literal: "Moreover, the reason I have withdrawn the army to Bashang is to wait until the feudal lords arrive and fix our covenants.", idiomatic: "I withdrew to Bashang only to wait until the lords arrive and we settle our covenants." },
  { zh: "」乃使人與秦吏行縣、鄉、邑，告諭之。", literal: "\" He then sent men with Qin clerks through counties, districts, and townships to announce and instruct them.", idiomatic: "\" He sent men with Qin clerks through every county, district, and township to proclaim it." },
  { zh: "秦民大喜。", literal: "The people of Qin were greatly pleased.", idiomatic: "The people of Qin rejoiced." },
  { zh: "爭持牛、羊、酒食獻饗軍士。", literal: "They vied to bring oxen, sheep, wine, and food to present and feast the soldiers.", idiomatic: "They vied to bring oxen, sheep, wine, and food to feast the troops." },
  { zh: "沛公又讓不受，曰：「倉粟多，非乏，不欲費民。", literal: "The Duke of Pei again declined and would not accept, saying: \"The granaries hold much grain; we are not in want and do not wish to burden the people.", idiomatic: "The Duke of Pei refused again: \"The granaries are full—we are not in want, and I will not burden the people.\"" },
  { zh: "」民又益喜，唯恐沛公不為秦王。", literal: "\" The people were all the more pleased, and feared only that the Duke of Pei would not become king of Qin.", idiomatic: "\" The people rejoiced all the more—and feared only that he would not become king of Qin." },
  { zh: "2項羽既定河北，率諸侯兵欲西入關。", literal: "2. Xiang Yu, having already settled Hebei, led the feudal lords' troops intending to enter the passes from the west.", idiomatic: "2. Xiang Yu, Hebei pacified, led the allied armies west toward the passes." },
  { zh: "先是，諸侯吏卒、繇使、屯戍過秦中者，秦中吏卒遇之多無狀。", literal: "Earlier, whenever officers and soldiers of the feudal lords, corvée laborers, and garrison troops passed through Guanzhong, the officers and soldiers of Guanzhong met them with much ill conduct.", idiomatic: "Before this, whenever allied officers, corvée men, or garrison troops passed through Guanzhong, the Qin soldiers they met behaved abominably." },
  { zh: "及章邯以秦軍降諸侯，諸侯吏卒乘勝多奴虜使之，輕折辱秦吏卒。", literal: "When Zhang Han surrendered the Qin army to the feudal lords, the allied officers and soldiers, riding their victory, often enslaved and used them and lightly humiliated the Qin officers and soldiers.", idiomatic: "When Zhang Han surrendered the Qin army, allied soldiers, drunk on victory, enslaved them wholesale and heaped humiliation on Qin officers and men." },
  { zh: "秦吏卒多怨，竊言曰：「章將軍等詐吾屬降諸侯。", literal: "The Qin officers and soldiers harbored much resentment and whispered among themselves: \"Generals Zhang and the rest tricked our company into surrendering to the feudal lords.", idiomatic: "Qin officers and men nursed bitter grievances and whispered: \"Zhang and the rest tricked us into surrendering to the allies." },
  { zh: "今能入關破秦，大善；", literal: "If we can now enter the passes and break Qin, that would be excellent;", idiomatic: "If we can enter the passes now and break Qin, well and good;" },
  { zh: "即不能，諸侯虜吾屬而東，秦又盡誅吾父母妻子，奈何？", literal: "if we cannot, the feudal lords will carry off our company eastward while Qin executes all our fathers, mothers, wives, and children—what then?", idiomatic: "if not, the allies will drag us east while Qin executes our fathers, mothers, wives, and children—what then?\"" },
  { zh: "」諸將微聞其計，以告項羽。", literal: "\" The generals caught faint word of their plot and reported it to Xiang Yu.", idiomatic: "\" The generals caught wind of the plot and told Xiang Yu." },
  { zh: "項羽召黥布、蒲將軍計曰：「秦吏卒尚眾，其心不服，至關不聽，事必危。", literal: "Xiang Yu summoned Qing Bu and General Pu to counsel, saying: \"The Qin officers and soldiers are still numerous; their hearts are not submissive. If they reach the passes and will not obey, the affair is sure to turn perilous.", idiomatic: "Xiang Yu called Qing Bu and General Pu to counsel: \"Qin soldiers are still many and their hearts are not ours. At the passes they will refuse to obey—the affair will turn deadly." },
  { zh: "不如擊殺之，而獨與章邯、長史欣、都尉翳入秦。", literal: "Better to strike and kill them, and enter Qin with Zhang Han, Chief Clerk Xin, and Commandant Yi alone.", idiomatic: "Better strike them down, and enter Qin with Zhang Han, Chief Clerk Xin, and Commandant Yi alone." },
  { zh: "」於是楚軍夜擊坑秦卒二十餘萬人新安城南。", literal: "\" Thereupon the Chu army struck by night and buried alive more than two hundred thousand Qin soldiers south of Xinan city.", idiomatic: "\" That night the Chu army struck and buried more than two hundred thousand Qin soldiers alive south of Xinan." },
  { zh: "或說沛公曰：「秦富十倍天下，地形強。", literal: "Someone advised the Duke of Pei, saying: \"Qin is ten times richer than all the rest under Heaven, and its terrain is strong.", idiomatic: "Someone urged the Duke of Pei: \"Qin is ten times wealthier than the rest of the realm, and its terrain is strong." },
  { zh: "聞項羽號章邯為雍王，王關中，今則來，沛公恐不得有此。", literal: "I hear Xiang Yu has styled Zhang Han King of Yong and made him king in Guanzhong; he is coming now, and the Duke of Pei may fear he will not keep this.", idiomatic: "Xiang Yu has made Zhang Han King of Yong over Guanzhong. He is coming now—you may lose everything." },
  { zh: "可急使兵守函谷關，無內諸侯軍；", literal: "You may urgently send troops to hold Hangu Pass and not admit the feudal lords' armies;", idiomatic: "Send troops at once to hold Hangu Pass and admit no allied army;" },
  { zh: "稍征關中兵以自益，距之。", literal: "gradually levy Guanzhong troops to strengthen yourself and resist them.", idiomatic: "levy Guanzhong's forces to strengthen yourself and hold them off." },
  { zh: "」沛公然其計，從之。", literal: "\" The Duke of Pei thought the plan sound and followed it.", idiomatic: "\" The Duke of Pei thought it sound and did as advised." },
  { zh: "已而項羽至關，關門閉。", literal: "Before long Xiang Yu reached the pass; the gate was shut.", idiomatic: "Soon Xiang Yu reached the pass—and found the gates closed." },
  { zh: "聞沛公已定關中，大怒，使黥布等攻破函谷關。", literal: "Hearing that the Duke of Pei had already secured Guanzhong, he was greatly enraged and ordered Qing Bu and the rest to break through Hangu Pass.", idiomatic: "Learning that the Duke of Pei had already taken Guanzhong, he flew into a rage and sent Qing Bu to break the pass." },
  { zh: "十二月，項羽進至戲。", literal: "In the twelfth month Xiang Yu advanced to Xi.", idiomatic: "In the twelfth month Xiang Yu advanced to Xi." },
  { zh: "沛公左司馬曹無傷使人言項羽曰：「沛公欲王關中，令子嬰為相，珍寶盡有之。", literal: "The Duke of Pei's Left Major, Cao Wushang, sent a man to tell Xiang Yu: \"The Duke of Pei wishes to be king in Guanzhong, to make Ziying his chancellor, and to keep all the treasures for himself.", idiomatic: "The Duke of Pei's Left Major, Cao Wushang, sent word to Xiang Yu: \"The Duke of Pei means to be king in Guanzhong, make Ziying his chancellor, and keep every treasure for himself.\"" },
  { zh: "」欲以求封。", literal: "\" He wished thereby to win a fief.", idiomatic: "\" He hoped thereby to win a fief." },
  { zh: "項羽大怒，饗士卒，期旦日擊沛公軍。", literal: "Xiang Yu was greatly enraged, feasted his soldiers, and set the morrow to strike the Duke of Pei's army.", idiomatic: "Xiang Yu raged, feasted his troops, and set the morrow to destroy the Duke of Pei's army." },
  { zh: "當是時，項羽兵四十萬，號百萬，在新豐鴻門；", literal: "At that time Xiang Yu's army was four hundred thousand, styled a million, at Hong Gate in Xinfeng;", idiomatic: "At that time Xiang Yu had four hundred thousand men—he called them a million—at Hong Gate in Xinfeng;" },
  { zh: "沛公兵十萬，號二十萬，在霸上。", literal: "the Duke of Pei's army was one hundred thousand, styled two hundred thousand, at Bashang.", idiomatic: "the Duke of Pei had one hundred thousand—he called them two hundred thousand—at Bashang." },
  { zh: "范增說項羽曰：「沛公居山東時，貪財好色。", literal: "Fan Zeng urged Xiang Yu, saying: \"When the Duke of Pei dwelt east of the mountains he was greedy for wealth and fond of women.", idiomatic: "Fan Zeng urged Xiang Yu: \"East of the mountains the Duke of Pei was greedy for gold and fond of women." },
  { zh: "今入關，財物無所取，婦女無所幸，此其志不在小。", literal: "Now, having entered the passes, he takes no goods and enjoys no women—his intent is not small.", idiomatic: "Now in the passes he takes no goods and enjoys no women. His ambition is no small thing." },
  { zh: "吾令人望其氣，皆為龍虎，成五采，此天子氣也。", literal: "I had men observe his aura: it is all dragon and tiger, forming the five colors—this is the aura of a Son of Heaven.", idiomatic: "I had his aura watched: dragon and tiger, the five colors mingled—the aura of a Son of Heaven." },
  { zh: "急擊勿失！", literal: "Strike quickly and do not let the chance slip!", idiomatic: "Strike now—do not let the chance slip!\"" },
  { zh: "楚左尹項伯者，項羽季父也，素善張良，乃夜馳之沛公軍，私見張良，具告以事，欲呼與俱去，曰：「毋俱死也！", literal: "Xiang Bo, Left Minister of Chu and Xiang Yu's uncle, had long been friendly with Zhang Liang; he galloped by night to the Duke of Pei's army, met Zhang Liang in private, and told him the whole affair, wishing to call him to flee together, saying: \"Do not die together!", idiomatic: "Xiang Bo, Left Minister of Chu and Xiang Yu's uncle, had long been close to Zhang Liang. He galloped by night to the Duke of Pei's camp, met Zhang Liang in secret, told him everything, and urged him to flee together: \"Do not die with them!\"" },
  { zh: "」張良曰：「臣為韓王送沛公。", literal: "\" Zhang Liang said: \"Your servant was sent by the king of Han to escort the Duke of Pei.", idiomatic: "\" Zhang Liang said: \"I was sent by the king of Han to serve the Duke of Pei." },
  { zh: "沛公今有急，亡去不義，不可不語。", literal: "The Duke of Pei is now in peril; to flee would be unrighteous—I cannot fail to speak.", idiomatic: "He is in peril now. To flee would be unrighteous. I must tell him.\"" },
  { zh: "」良乃入，具告沛公。", literal: "\" Liang then entered and told the Duke of Pei the whole matter.", idiomatic: "\" Liang went in and told the Duke of Pei everything." },
  { zh: "沛公大驚。", literal: "The Duke of Pei was greatly alarmed.", idiomatic: "The Duke of Pei was stricken with alarm." },
  { zh: "良曰：「料公士卒足以當項羽乎？", literal: "Liang said: \"Does my lord judge his soldiers sufficient to match Xiang Yu?", idiomatic: "Liang said: \"Do you judge your soldiers a match for Xiang Yu?\"" },
  { zh: "」沛公默然曰：「固不如也。", literal: "\" The Duke of Pei was silent, then said: \"They are certainly not equal.", idiomatic: "\" The Duke of Pei was silent. \"They are not,\" he said at last." },
  { zh: "且為之奈何？", literal: "What is to be done?", idiomatic: "What can be done?\"" },
  { zh: "」張良曰：「請往謂項伯，言沛公之不敢叛也。", literal: "\" Zhang Liang said: \"Please let me go tell Xiang Bo that the Duke of Pei does not dare rebel.", idiomatic: "\" Zhang Liang said: \"Let me tell Xiang Bo that you do not dare rebel.\"" },
  { zh: "」沛公曰：「君安與項伯有故？", literal: "\" The Duke of Pei said: \"How do you and Xiang Bo share an old tie?", idiomatic: "\" The Duke of Pei said: \"How do you know Xiang Bo?\"" },
  { zh: "」張良曰：「秦時與臣游，嘗殺人，臣活之。", literal: "\" Zhang Liang said: \"In Qin times we were companions; he once killed a man, and your servant saved his life.", idiomatic: "\" Zhang Liang said: \"In Qin times we were companions. He once killed a man, and I saved his life." },
  { zh: "今事有急，故幸來告良。", literal: "Now the affair is urgent, and so he has come in fortune to tell Liang.", idiomatic: "Now the crisis is upon us, and he has come to warn me.\"" },
  { zh: "」沛公曰：「孰與君少長？", literal: "\" The Duke of Pei said: \"Which of you is the elder?", idiomatic: "\" The Duke of Pei said: \"Which of you is older?\"" },
  { zh: "」良曰：「長於臣。", literal: "\" Liang said: \"He is older than your servant.", idiomatic: "\" Liang said: \"He is older than I.\"" },
  { zh: "」沛公曰：「君為我呼入，吾得兄事之。", literal: "\" The Duke of Pei said: \"Summon him in for me; I shall treat him as an elder brother.", idiomatic: "\" The Duke of Pei said: \"Bring him in. I shall treat him as an elder brother.\"" },
  { zh: "」張良出，固要項伯；", literal: "\" Zhang Liang went out and earnestly invited Xiang Bo;", idiomatic: "\" Zhang Liang went out and pressed Xiang Bo to enter;" },
  { zh: "項伯即入見沛公。", literal: "Xiang Bo at once entered to see the Duke of Pei.", idiomatic: "and Xiang Bo entered at once to see the Duke of Pei." },
  { zh: "沛公奉卮酒為壽，約為婚姻，曰：「吾入關，秋毫不敢有所近，籍吏民，封府庫而待將軍。", literal: "The Duke of Pei offered a cup of wine to wish him long life, pledged marriage between their houses, and said: \"When I entered the passes I did not dare touch the slightest thing; I registered clerks and people, sealed the treasuries, and wait for the general.", idiomatic: "The Duke of Pei offered wine to wish him long life, pledged marriage between their houses, and said: \"When I entered the passes I touched nothing—not the smallest thing. I registered clerks and people, sealed the treasuries, and wait for the general." },
  { zh: "所以遣將守關者，備他盜之出入與非常也。", literal: "The reason I sent generals to hold the pass is to guard against other robbers entering and leaving and against emergencies.", idiomatic: "I posted men at the pass only to guard against robbers and emergencies." },
  { zh: "日夜望將軍至，豈敢反乎！", literal: "Day and night I have looked for the general to arrive—how would I dare rebel!", idiomatic: "Day and night I have watched for your arrival—how would I dare rebel!\"" },
  { zh: "願伯具言臣之不敢倍德也。", literal: "I beg Bo to tell in full that your servant does not dare betray virtue.", idiomatic: "Tell him fully that I do not dare betray his grace.\"" },
  { zh: "」項伯許諾，謂沛公曰：「旦日不可不蚤自來謝。", literal: "\" Xiang Bo agreed and told the Duke of Pei: \"Tomorrow you must come early in person to apologize.", idiomatic: "\" Xiang Bo agreed. \"Tomorrow you must come early in person to apologize.\"" },
  { zh: "」沛公曰：「諾。", literal: "\" The Duke of Pei said: \"Agreed.", idiomatic: "\" The Duke of Pei said: \"I will.\"" },
  { zh: "」於是項伯復夜去，至軍中，具以沛公言報項羽，因言曰：「沛公不先破關中，公豈敢入乎？", literal: "\" Thereupon Xiang Bo returned by night to the army, reported the Duke of Pei's words fully to Xiang Yu, and added: \"If the Duke of Pei had not broken Guanzhong first, how would you dare enter?", idiomatic: "\" Xiang Bo rode back by night, told Xiang Yu everything the Duke of Pei had said, and added: \"If the Duke of Pei had not broken Guanzhong first, how would you have dared enter?" },
  { zh: "今人有大功而擊之，不義也。", literal: "Now, when a man has great merit and you strike him, it is unrighteous.", idiomatic: "To strike a man of great merit is unrighteous." },
  { zh: "不如因善遇之。", literal: "Better to treat him well because of it.", idiomatic: "Better treat him generously.\"" },
  { zh: "」項羽許諾。", literal: "\" Xiang Yu agreed.", idiomatic: "\" Xiang Yu agreed." },
  { zh: "沛公旦日從百餘騎來見項羽鴻門，謝曰：「臣與將軍戮力而攻秦，將軍戰河北，臣戰河南。", literal: "At dawn the Duke of Pei came with a little more than a hundred riders to see Xiang Yu at Hong Gate and apologized, saying: \"Your servant and the general joined strength to attack Qin; the general fought in Hebei, your servant in Henan.", idiomatic: "At dawn the Duke of Pei came with a little more than a hundred riders to Hong Gate, apologized to Xiang Yu, and said: \"My lord and I joined strength against Qin—you fought in Hebei, I in Henan." },
  { zh: "不自意能先入關破秦，得復見將軍於此。", literal: "I did not expect in my own mind to enter the passes first and break Qin, and to meet the general again here.", idiomatic: "I never expected to enter the passes first, break Qin, and meet you again here." },
  { zh: "今者有小人之言，令將軍與臣有隙。", literal: "Now there have been the words of petty men, causing a rift between the general and your servant.", idiomatic: "Now petty men's words have set a rift between us.\"" },
  { zh: "」項羽曰：「此沛公左司馬曹無傷言之，不然，籍何以生此！", literal: "\" Xiang Yu said: \"This was spoken by the Duke of Pei's Left Major, Cao Wushang; otherwise, how would Yu have come to this!", idiomatic: "\" Xiang Yu said: \"That was the Duke of Pei's Left Major, Cao Wushang—not otherwise. How else would I have come to this!\"" },
  { zh: "」項羽因留沛公與飲。", literal: "\" Xiang Yu then detained the Duke of Pei to drink with him.", idiomatic: "\" Xiang Yu kept the Duke of Pei to drink with him." },
  { zh: "范增數目項羽，舉所佩玉□夬以示之者三。", literal: "Fan Zeng repeatedly signaled Xiang Yu with his eyes and raised the jade□ ring he wore, showing it three times.", idiomatic: "Fan Zeng signaled Xiang Yu again and again with his eyes and three times raised the jade□ ring at his belt." },
  { zh: "項羽默然不應。", literal: "Xiang Yu was silent and did not respond.", idiomatic: "Xiang Yu stayed silent and would not answer." },
  { zh: "范增起，出，召項莊，謂曰：「君王為人不忍。", literal: "Fan Zeng rose, went out, summoned Xiang Zhuang, and said to him: \"The king's nature is not hard enough.", idiomatic: "Fan Zeng rose, went out, called Xiang Zhuang, and said: \"Our lord's heart is not hard enough." },
  { zh: "若入前為壽，壽畢，以劍舞，因擊沛公於坐，殺之。", literal: "If you enter, advance to offer a toast for long life; when the toast is done, dance with the sword and strike the Duke of Pei in his seat and kill him.", idiomatic: "Go in, offer a toast for long life, and when it is done dance with your sword—strike the Duke of Pei where he sits and kill him." },
  { zh: "不者，若屬皆且為所虜！", literal: "If not, you lot will all soon be made captives!", idiomatic: "If you fail, every one of you will be taken captive!\"" },
  { zh: "」莊則入為壽，壽畢，曰：「軍中無以為樂，請以劍舞。", literal: "\" Zhuang then entered to offer the toast for long life; when it was done he said: \"In the army there is nothing for amusement—I beg to dance with the sword.", idiomatic: "\" Zhuang entered, offered the toast, and when it was done said: \"The camp lacks amusement—I beg leave to dance with my sword.\"" },
  { zh: "」項羽曰：「諾。", literal: "\" Xiang Yu said: \"Agreed.", idiomatic: "\" Xiang Yu said: \"Very well.\"" },
  { zh: "」項莊拔劍起舞。", literal: "” Xiang Zhuang drew his sword and began to dance.", idiomatic: "” Xiang Zhuang drew his sword and danced." },
  { zh: "項伯亦拔劍起舞，常以身翼蔽沛公，莊不得擊。", literal: "Xiang Bo also drew his sword and danced, often shielding the Lord of Pei with his body like wings; Zhuang could not strike.", idiomatic: "Xiang Bo also drew his sword and danced, repeatedly shielding the Lord of Pei with his body; Zhuang could not land a blow." },
  { zh: "於是張良至軍門見樊噲。", literal: "Thereupon Zhang Liang went to the camp gate and saw Fan Kuai.", idiomatic: "Zhang Liang then went to the camp gate and met Fan Kuai." },
  { zh: "噲曰：「今日之事何如？", literal: "Kuai said: “How are today’s affairs?", idiomatic: "Fan Kuai said, “How do things stand today?" },
  { zh: "」良曰：「今項莊拔劍舞，其意常在沛公也。", literal: "” Liang said: “Now Xiang Zhuang is dancing with drawn sword; his intent is constantly on the Lord of Pei.”", idiomatic: "” Zhang Liang said, “Xiang Zhuang is dancing with his sword drawn—his aim is always at the Lord of Pei.”" },
  { zh: "」噲曰：「此迫矣，臣請入，與之同命！", literal: "” Kuai said: “This is urgent! Your servant asks to enter and share life or death with him!”", idiomatic: "” Fan Kuai said, “This is desperate! I beg to go in and stake my life with his!”" },
  { zh: "」噲即帶劍擁盾入。", literal: "” Kuai immediately took sword and shield and entered.", idiomatic: "” Fan Kuai at once entered with sword and shield." },
  { zh: "軍門衛士欲止不內，樊噲側其盾以撞，衛士僕地。", literal: "The camp-gate guards wished to stop him and not admit him; Fan Kuai tilted his shield and rammed them; the guards fell to the ground.", idiomatic: "The gate guards tried to block him; Fan Kuai angled his shield and charged; the guards fell sprawling." },
  { zh: "遂入，披帷立，瞋目視項羽，頭髮上指，目眥盡裂。", literal: "He then entered, parted the curtain, and stood; glaring at Xiang Yu, his hair bristled upward and his eye corners split to the limit.", idiomatic: "He entered, pushed aside the curtain, and stood glaring at Xiang Yu, hair bristling on end and eyes bloodshot to the corners." },
  { zh: "項羽按劍而跽曰：「客何為者？", literal: "Xiang Yu pressed his sword and rose on his knees, saying: “Guest, what are you doing?", idiomatic: "Xiang Yu hand on sword, rose to his knees and said, “Stranger, what do you want?" },
  { zh: "」張良曰：「沛公之參乘樊噲也。", literal: "” Zhang Liang said: “He is Fan Kuai, the Lord of Pei’s outrider.”", idiomatic: "” Zhang Liang said, “He is Fan Kuai, the Lord of Pei’s outrider.”" },
  { zh: "」項羽曰：「壯士！", literal: "” Xiang Yu said: “Brave man!", idiomatic: "” Xiang Yu said, “A brave man!" },
  { zh: "賜之卮酒！", literal: "Grant him a cup of wine!”", idiomatic: "Give him a cup of wine!”" },
  { zh: "」則與斗卮酒。", literal: "” He was given a dou-measure cup of wine.", idiomatic: "” They gave him a full cup of wine." },
  { zh: "噲拜謝，起，立而飲之。", literal: "Kuai bowed in thanks, rose, stood, and drank it.", idiomatic: "Fan Kuai bowed his thanks, rose, stood, and drained it." },
  { zh: "項羽曰：「賜之彘肩。", literal: "Xiang Yu said: “Grant him a pork shoulder.", idiomatic: "Xiang Yu said, “Give him a pork shoulder." },
  { zh: "」則與一生彘肩。", literal: "” He was given a whole raw pork shoulder.", idiomatic: "” They gave him a whole raw pork shoulder." },
  { zh: "樊噲覆其盾於地，加彘肩其上，拔劍切而啖之。", literal: "Fan Kuai turned his shield upside down on the ground, set the pork shoulder on it, drew his sword, sliced it, and ate.", idiomatic: "Fan Kuai set his shield on the ground, laid the shoulder on it, drew his sword, cut it up, and ate." },
  { zh: "項羽曰：「壯士能復飲乎？", literal: "Xiang Yu said: “Brave man, can you drink again?", idiomatic: "Xiang Yu said, “Brave man, can you drink more?" },
  { zh: "」樊噲曰：「臣死且不避，卮酒安足辭？", literal: "” Fan Kuai said: “Your servant would not shrink from death—how could a cup of wine be worth declining?", idiomatic: "” Fan Kuai said, “I would not shrink from death—why refuse a cup of wine?" },
  { zh: "夫秦有虎狼之心，殺人如不能舉，刑人如恐不勝；", literal: "Qin had the heart of tiger and wolf; killing men as though unable to exhaust the effort, punishing men as though fearing not to exceed;", idiomatic: "Qin had a tiger-and-wolf heart—killing men as if it could never kill enough, punishing men as if it feared not to exceed every limit;" },
  { zh: "天下皆叛之。", literal: "all under Heaven turned against it.", idiomatic: "all under Heaven turned against it." },
  { zh: "懷王與諸將約曰：『先破秦入咸陽者，王之。", literal: "King Huai made a pact with the generals, saying: ‘Whoever first breaks Qin and enters Xianyang shall be made king.", idiomatic: "King Huai agreed with the generals: ‘Whoever first defeats Qin and enters Xianyang shall be king." },
  { zh: "』今沛公先破秦入咸陽，豪毛不敢有所近，還軍霸上以待將軍。", literal: "’ Now the Lord of Pei was first to break Qin and enter Xianyang; he dared not touch even a hair’s breadth of gain, withdrew his army to Bashang to await the general.", idiomatic: "’ The Lord of Pei was first to defeat Qin and enter Xianyang; he did not dare touch the slightest thing, withdrew his army to Bashang to await Your Lordship." },
  { zh: "勞苦而功高如此，未有封爵之賞，而聽細人之說，欲誅有功之人，此亡秦之續耳，竊為將軍不取也！", literal: "With toil and merit so high, there is no reward of enfeoffment, yet you heed petty men’s words and wish to execute men with merit—this is the continuation of Qin’s destruction; I venture to say it is not what the general should take!”", idiomatic: "After such labor and such merit, there is no enfeoffment—yet you heed petty men and would kill men of merit. This continues Qin’s way; I venture it is not what Your Lordship should do!”" },
  { zh: "」項羽未有以應，曰：「坐！", literal: "” Xiang Yu had nothing with which to reply and said: “Sit!", idiomatic: "” Xiang Yu had no answer and said, “Sit!" },
  { zh: "」樊噲從良坐。", literal: "” Fan Kuai followed Liang and sat.", idiomatic: "” Fan Kuai sat with Zhang Liang." },
  { zh: "坐須臾，沛公起如廁，因招樊噲出。", literal: "After sitting a little while, the Lord of Pei rose as if to the privy and thereupon summoned Fan Kuai out.", idiomatic: "After a short while the Lord of Pei rose as if for the privy and beckoned Fan Kuai out." },
  { zh: "公曰：「今者出，未辭也，為之奈何？", literal: "The lord said: “Now that we have gone out, we have not taken leave—what is to be done?", idiomatic: "The Lord of Pei said, “We have left without farewell—what shall we do?" },
  { zh: "」樊噲曰：「如今人方為刀俎，我方為魚肉，何辭為？", literal: "” Fan Kuai said: “Now others are just the chopping block and cleaver, while we are the fish and meat—why take leave?", idiomatic: "” Fan Kuai said, “They are the cleaver and we are the meat on the block—why bother with farewells?" },
  { zh: "」於是遂去。", literal: "” They thereupon departed.", idiomatic: "” They left at once." },
  { zh: "鴻門去霸上四十里，沛公則置車騎，脫身獨騎；", literal: "Hong Gate was forty li from Bashang; the Lord of Pei left his chariot and horsemen and escaped alone on horseback;", idiomatic: "Hong Gate was forty li from Bashang; the Lord of Pei left his chariot and escort and rode off alone;" },
  { zh: "樊噲、夏侯嬰、靳強、紀信等四人持劍、盾步走，從驪山下道芷陽，間行趣霸上。", literal: "Fan Kuai, Xiahou Ying, Jin Qiang, Ji Xin, and four others carried sword and shield and walked, taking the road down from Mount Li through Zhiyang, traveling by bypaths to hurry to Bashang.", idiomatic: "Fan Kuai, Xiahou Ying, Jin Qiang, and Ji Xin and the others went on foot with swords and shields, taking the road down from Mount Li through Zhiyang by secret paths to reach Bashang." },
  { zh: "留張良使謝項羽，以白璧獻羽，玉斗與亞父。", literal: "He left Zhang Liang to apologize to Xiang Yu, presenting the white jade disc to Yu and the jade goblet to the Senior Lord.", idiomatic: "He left Zhang Liang to make his excuses to Xiang Yu, offering the white jade disc to Yu and the jade goblet to the Senior Lord." },
  { zh: "沛公謂良曰：「從此道至吾軍，不過二十里耳。", literal: "The Lord of Pei told Liang: “From this road to my army is no more than twenty li.", idiomatic: "The Lord of Pei told Zhang Liang, “From this road to my camp is no more than twenty li." },
  { zh: "度我至軍中，公乃入。", literal: "Estimate when I have reached the army, then enter.”", idiomatic: "When you judge I have reached camp, then go in.”" },
  { zh: "」沛公已去，間至軍中，張良入謝曰：「沛公不勝杯杓，不能辭，謹使臣良奉白璧一雙，再拜獻將軍足下；", literal: "” The Lord of Pei had already gone and reached the army by bypaths; Zhang Liang entered to apologize, saying: “The Lord of Pei could not bear the cups and ladles and could not take leave; he respectfully sends your servant Liang to present a pair of white jade discs, bowing twice to offer them at the general’s feet;", idiomatic: "” The Lord of Pei was already gone and had reached camp by a side path; Zhang Liang went in to apologize: “The Lord of Pei could not hold his wine and could not take his leave; he respectfully sends me with a pair of white jade discs, bowing twice to present them to Your Lordship;" },
  { zh: "玉斗一雙，再拜奉亞父足下。", literal: "a pair of jade goblets, bowing twice to present them at the Senior Lord’s feet.", idiomatic: "and a pair of jade goblets, bowing twice to present them to the Senior Lord.”" },
  { zh: "」項羽曰：「沛公安在？", literal: "” Xiang Yu said: “Where is the Lord of Pei?", idiomatic: "” Xiang Yu said, “Where is the Lord of Pei?" },
  { zh: "」良曰：「聞將軍有意督過之，脫身獨去，已至軍矣。", literal: "” Liang said: “Hearing that the general intended to reprove him for faults, he slipped away alone and has already reached his army.”", idiomatic: "” Zhang Liang said, “Hearing that Your Lordship meant to hold him to account, he slipped away alone and is already at his camp.”" },
  { zh: "」項羽則受璧，置之坐上。", literal: "” Xiang Yu then accepted the disc and set it on his seat.", idiomatic: "” Xiang Yu accepted the disc and set it on his seat." },
  { zh: "亞父受玉斗，置之地，拔劍撞而破之，曰：「唉！", literal: "The Senior Lord received the jade goblet, set it on the ground, drew his sword and smashed it, saying: “Alas!", idiomatic: "The Senior Lord took the jade goblet, set it on the ground, drew his sword and smashed it, crying, “Alas!" },
  { zh: "豎子不足與謀！", literal: "The stripling is not worth plotting with!", idiomatic: "That boy is not worth plotting with!" },
  { zh: "奪將軍天下者，必沛公也。", literal: "He who will seize the general’s empire under Heaven will surely be the Lord of Pei.", idiomatic: "The one who will take Your Lordship’s empire will surely be the Lord of Pei." },
  { zh: "吾屬今為之虜矣！", literal: "We are about to become his captives!”", idiomatic: "We are all about to become his prisoners!”" },
  { zh: "」沛公至軍，立誅殺曹無傷。", literal: "” When the Lord of Pei reached his army, he immediately executed Cao Wushang.", idiomatic: "” When the Lord of Pei reached camp, he had Cao Wushang executed at once." },
  { zh: "居數日，項羽引兵西，屠咸陽，殺秦降王子嬰，燒秦宮室，火三月不滅。", literal: "After several days, Xiang Yu led his troops west, slaughtered Xianyang, killed the surrendered King of Qin Ziying, burned the Qin palaces—the fire did not die for three months.", idiomatic: "Several days later Xiang Yu marched west, sacked Xianyang, killed the surrendered King of Qin Ziying, and burned the Qin palaces; the fires burned for three months." },
  { zh: "收其貨寶、婦女而東。", literal: "He gathered its valuables, treasures, and women and went east.", idiomatic: "He gathered its treasure and women and marched east." },
  { zh: "秦民大失望。", literal: "The people of Qin were greatly disappointed.", idiomatic: "The people of Qin were deeply disappointed." },
  { zh: "韓生說項羽曰：「關中阻山帶河，四塞之地，地肥饒，可都以霸。", literal: "Han Sheng advised Xiang Yu, saying: “Within the Passes, mountains block and rivers gird—it is a land closed on four sides, the soil rich and fertile; one may make it capital and hegemon.", idiomatic: "Han Sheng urged Xiang Yu: “The land within the Passes is barred by mountains and girded by rivers—a fortress on four sides, rich soil; you could make it your capital and rule as hegemon." },
  { zh: "」項羽見秦宮室皆已燒殘破，又心思東歸，曰：「富貴不歸故鄉，如衣繡夜行，誰知之者？", literal: "” Xiang Yu, seeing that the Qin palaces were all already burned and ruined, and his mind set on returning east, said: “Wealth and honor without returning to one’s homeland is like wearing brocade by night—who would know?", idiomatic: "” Xiang Yu saw the Qin palaces already burned and ruined, and his heart was set on going east; he said, “Wealth and honor without returning home is like wearing brocade at night—who would know?" },
  { zh: "」韓生退曰：「人言楚人沐猴而冠耳，果然！", literal: "” Han Sheng withdrew, saying: “Men say Chu men are monkeys bathed and capped—and so it proves!", idiomatic: "” Han Sheng withdrew, muttering, “They say Chu men are monkeys dressed in caps—and how true!”" },
  { zh: "」項羽聞之，烹韓生。", literal: "” Xiang Yu heard it and boiled Han Sheng alive.", idiomatic: "” Xiang Yu heard of it and had Han Sheng boiled alive." },
  { zh: "3項羽使人致命懷王，懷王曰：「如約。", literal: "3. Xiang Yu sent a man to report to King Huai; King Huai said: “As per the pact.", idiomatic: "3. Xiang Yu sent word to King Huai; King Huai said, “As agreed." },
  { zh: "」項羽怒曰：「懷王者，吾家所立耳，非有功伐，何以得專主約？", literal: "” Xiang Yu angrily said: “King Huai was established by my house alone—not through merit in campaigning; how can he alone control the pact?", idiomatic: "” Xiang Yu raged: “King Huai was enthroned by my family—not for merit in the field; how can he alone dictate the pact?" },
  { zh: "天下初發難時，假立諸侯後以伐秦。", literal: "When the empire first rose in revolt, we set up the descendants of the feudal lords in name to attack Qin.", idiomatic: "When the revolt first began, we set up the lords’ descendants in name to attack Qin." },
  { zh: "然身被堅執銳首事，暴露於野三年，滅秦定天下者，皆將相諸君與籍之力也。", literal: "Yet I myself wore armor and grasped sharp weapons as the first to take the field, exposed in the wilds three years—those who destroyed Qin and settled the empire are all through the effort of you generals and ministers and Ji’s strength.", idiomatic: "Yet I wore armor and bore arms from the start, exposed in the field three years—destroying Qin and settling the empire was the work of you generals and ministers and of Ji." },
  { zh: "懷王雖無功，固當分其地而王之。", literal: "Though King Huai had no merit, he should still be given a share of territory and made king.”", idiomatic: "King Huai had no merit, yet he should still receive a share of land and be made king.”" },
  { zh: "」諸將皆曰：「善！", literal: "” The generals all said: “Good!", idiomatic: "” The generals all said, “Well said!" },
  { zh: "」春，正月，羽陽尊懷王為義帝，曰：「古之帝者，地方千里，必居上游。", literal: "” In spring, the first month, Yu at Yang honored King Huai as the Emperor of Righteousness, saying: “Ancient emperors held a thousand li of territory and must dwell on the upper reaches.", idiomatic: "” In spring, the first month, at Yang, Yu honored King Huai as Emperor Yi, saying, “Ancient emperors held a thousand li and had to dwell upstream." },
  { zh: "」乃徙義帝於江南，都郴。", literal: "” He then moved the Emperor of Righteousness to the lands south of the Yangzi, with his capital at Chen.", idiomatic: "” He moved Emperor Yi south of the Yangzi, with his capital at Chen." },
  { zh: "二月，羽分天下王諸將。", literal: "In the second month, Yu divided the empire and made the generals kings.", idiomatic: "In the second month, Yu divided the empire and enfeoffed the generals as kings." },
  { zh: "羽自立為西楚霸王，王梁、楚地九郡，都彭城。", literal: "Yu established himself as Hegemon-King of Western Chu, ruling the nine commanderies of Liang and Chu, with his capital at Pengcheng.", idiomatic: "Yu made himself Hegemon-King of Western Chu, ruling nine commanderies of Liang and Chu, with his capital at Pengcheng." },
  { zh: "羽與范增疑沛公，而業已講解，又惡負約，乃陰謀曰：「巴、蜀道險，秦之遷人皆居之。", literal: "Yu and Fan Zeng suspected the Lord of Pei, but since they had already made peace, and also loathed breaking the pact, they secretly plotted, saying: “Ba and Shu have perilous roads; Qin’s relocated people all dwell there.", idiomatic: "Yu and Fan Zeng distrusted the Lord of Pei; peace had been made, yet they hated to break the pact openly, so they plotted in secret: “Ba and Shu have treacherous roads; Qin’s exiles all live there." },
  { zh: "」乃曰：「巴、蜀亦關中地也。", literal: "” They then said: “Ba and Shu are also lands within the Passes.", idiomatic: "” They said, “Ba and Shu are also within the Passes." },
  { zh: "」故立沛公為漢王，王巴、蜀、漢中，都南鄭。", literal: "” Therefore they established the Lord of Pei as King of Han, ruling Ba, Shu, and Hanzhong, with his capital at Nanzheng.", idiomatic: "” So they made the Lord of Pei King of Han, ruling Ba, Shu, and Hanzhong, capital at Nanzheng." },
  { zh: "而三分關中，王秦降將，以距塞漢路。", literal: "They then divided Guanzhong into three parts and made Qin’s surrendered generals kings, to block and bar the Han road.", idiomatic: "They divided Guanzhong three ways and made Qin’s surrendered generals kings to block the Han." },
  { zh: "章邯為雍王，王咸陽以西，都廢丘。", literal: "Zhang Han became King of Yong, ruling west of Xianyang, with his capital at Feiqiu.", idiomatic: "Zhang Han was made King of Yong, ruling west of Xianyang, capital at Feiqiu." },
  { zh: "長史欣者，故為櫟陽獄掾，嘗有德於項梁；", literal: "Chief Clerk Xin had formerly been a prison clerk at Liyang and had once shown kindness to Xiang Liang;", idiomatic: "Chief Clerk Xin had been a prison clerk at Liyang and had once done Xiang Liang a kindness;" },
  { zh: "都尉董翳者，本勸章邯降楚。", literal: "Commandant Dong Yi had originally urged Zhang Han to surrender to Chu.", idiomatic: "Commandant Dong Yi had originally urged Zhang Han to surrender to Chu." },
  { zh: "故立欣為塞王，王咸陽以東，至河，都櫟陽；", literal: "Therefore Xin was established as King of Sai, ruling east of Xianyang to the river, with his capital at Liyang;", idiomatic: "So Xin was made King of Sai, ruling east of Xianyang to the Yellow River, capital at Liyang;" },
  { zh: "立翳為翟王，王上郡，都高奴。", literal: "Yi was established as King of Di, ruling Shang commandery, with his capital at Gaonu.", idiomatic: "Yi was made King of Di, ruling Shang commandery, capital at Gaonu." },
  { zh: "項羽欲自取梁地，乃徙魏王豹為西魏王，王河東，都平陽。", literal: "Xiang Yu wished to take Liang territory for himself; he therefore moved King Bao of Wei to be King of Western Wei, ruling Hedong, with his capital at Pingyang.", idiomatic: "Xiang Yu wanted Liang for himself, so he moved King Bao of Wei to Western Wei, ruling Hedong, capital at Pingyang." },
  { zh: "瑕丘申陽者，張耳嬖臣也，先下河南郡，迎楚河上，故立申陽為河南王，都洛陽。", literal: "Shen Yang of Xiaqiu was Zhang Er’s favorite minister; he had first taken Henan commandery and received Chu on the north bank of the river—therefore Shen Yang was established as King of Henan, with his capital at Luoyang.", idiomatic: "Shen Yang of Xiaqiu was Zhang Er’s favorite; he had first taken Henan and received Chu north of the river, so he was made King of Henan, capital at Luoyang." },
  { zh: "韓王成因故都，都陽翟。", literal: "King Cheng of Han kept his former capital, with his seat at Yangzhai.", idiomatic: "King Cheng of Han kept his former territory, capital at Yangzhai." },
  { zh: "趙將司馬卬定河內，數有功，故立卬為殷王，王河內，都朝歌。", literal: "The Zhao general Sima Ang settled Henei and had many merits—therefore Ang was established as King of Yin, ruling Henei, with his capital at Chaoge.", idiomatic: "The Zhao general Sima Ang had secured Henei with repeated merit, so Ang was made King of Yin, ruling Henei, capital at Chaoge." },
  { zh: "徙趙王歇為代王。", literal: "King Xie of Zhao was moved to be King of Dai.", idiomatic: "King Xie of Zhao was moved to Dai." },
  { zh: "趙相張耳素賢，又從入關，故立耳為常山王，王趙地，治襄國。", literal: "Zhao’s chancellor Zhang Er was by nature worthy and had also followed in entering the Passes—therefore Er was established as King of Changshan, ruling Zhao territory, administering Xiangguo.", idiomatic: "Zhao’s chancellor Zhang Er was known for worth and had entered the Passes with the army, so Er was made King of Changshan, ruling Zhao lands from Xiangguo." },
  { zh: "當陽君黥布為楚將，常冠軍，故立布為九江王，都六。", literal: "Lord Dangyang Qing Bu was a Chu general and often led the vanguard—therefore Bu was established as King of Jiujiang, with his capital at Lu.", idiomatic: "Lord Dangyang Ying Bu was a Chu general who often led the van, so Bu was made King of Jiujiang, capital at Lu." },
  { zh: "番君吳芮率百越佐諸侯，又從入關，故立芮為衡山王，都邾。", literal: "Lord Fan Wu Rui led the Hundred Yue in aiding the feudal lords and also followed in entering the Passes—therefore Rui was established as King of Hengshan, with his capital at Zhu.", idiomatic: "Lord Fan Wu Rui had led the Yue in aiding the allies and entered the Passes with them, so Rui was made King of Hengshan, capital at Zhu." },
  { zh: "義帝柱國共敖將軍擊南郡，功多，因立敖為臨江王，都江陵。", literal: "The Emperor of Righteousness’s pillar-of-state Gong Ao the general attacked Nan commandery with many achievements—therefore Ao was established as King of Linjiang, with his capital at Jiangling.", idiomatic: "Emperor Yi’s pillar Gong Ao had attacked Nan commandery with great merit, so Ao was made King of Linjiang, capital at Jiangling." },
  { zh: "徙燕王韓廣為遼東王，都無終。", literal: "King Guang of Yan was moved to be King of Liaodong, with his capital at Wuzhong.", idiomatic: "King Guang of Yan was moved to Liaodong, capital at Wuzhong." },
  { zh: "燕將臧荼從楚救趙，因從入關，故立荼為燕王，都薊。", literal: "The Yan general Zang Tu followed Chu to rescue Zhao and thereby followed in entering the Passes—therefore Tu was established as King of Yan, with his capital at Ji.", idiomatic: "The Yan general Zang Tu had marched with Chu to save Zhao and entered the Passes with them, so Tu was made King of Yan, capital at Ji." },
  { zh: "徙齊王田市為膠東王，都即墨。", literal: "King Shi of Qi was moved to be King of Jiaodong, with his capital at Jimo.", idiomatic: "King Shi of Qi was moved to Jiaodong, capital at Jimo." },
  { zh: "齊將田都從楚救趙，因從入關，故立都為齊王，都臨菑。", literal: "The Qi general Tian Du followed Chu to rescue Zhao and thereby followed in entering the Passes—therefore Du was established as King of Qi, with his capital at Linzi.", idiomatic: "The Qi general Tian Du had marched with Chu to save Zhao and entered the Passes with them, so Du was made King of Qi, capital at Linzi." },
  { zh: "項羽方渡河救趙，田安下濟北數城，引其兵降項羽，故立安為濟北王，都博陽。", literal: "When Xiang Yu was crossing the river to rescue Zhao, Tian An took several cities of Jibei and led his troops to surrender to Xiang Yu—therefore An was established as King of Jibei, with his capital at Boyang.", idiomatic: "While Xiang Yu was crossing the river to save Zhao, Tian An took several Jibei cities and brought his troops over to Yu, so An was made King of Jibei, capital at Boyang." },
  { zh: "田榮數負項梁，又不肯將兵從楚擊秦，以故不封。", literal: "Tian Rong had repeatedly failed Xiang Liang and also refused to lead troops with Chu to strike Qin—for this reason he was not enfeoffed.", idiomatic: "Tian Rong had repeatedly crossed Xiang Liang and refused to march with Chu against Qin, so he received no fief." },
  { zh: "成安君陳餘棄將印去，不從入關，亦不封。", literal: "Lord Cheng’an Chen Yu abandoned his general’s seal and left, did not follow in entering the Passes, and was also not enfeoffed.", idiomatic: "Lord Cheng’an Chen Yu had cast aside his general’s seal and left, did not enter the Passes, and was not enfeoffed either." },
  { zh: "客多說項羽曰：「張耳、陳餘，一體有功於趙，今耳為王，餘不可以不封。", literal: "Guests often urged Xiang Yu, saying: “Zhang Er and Chen Yu were as one body in merit to Zhao; now Er is king—Yu cannot go unenfeoffed.", idiomatic: "Advisers often told Xiang Yu: “Zhang Er and Chen Yu shared one merit for Zhao; Er is now king—Yu must not go without a fief." },
  { zh: "」羽不得已，聞其在南皮，因環封之三縣。", literal: "” Yu had no choice; hearing he was at Nanpi, he therefore enfeoffed him in a ring with three districts.", idiomatic: "” Yu reluctantly heard he was at Nanpi and enfeoffed him with three counties in a ring." },
  { zh: "番君將梅鋗功多，封十萬戶侯。", literal: "Lord Fan’s general Mei Xie had many achievements and was enfeoffed as marquis of one hundred thousand households.", idiomatic: "Lord Fan’s general Mei Xie had great merit and was made marquis of one hundred thousand households." },
  { zh: "4漢王怒，欲攻項羽，周勃、灌嬰、樊噲皆勸之。", literal: "4. The King of Han was angry and wished to attack Xiang Yu; Zhou Bo, Guan Ying, and Fan Kuai all urged him.", idiomatic: "4. The King of Han was furious and meant to attack Xiang Yu; Zhou Bo, Guan Ying, and Fan Kuai all dissuaded him." },
  { zh: "蕭何諫曰：「雖王漢中之惡，不猶愈於死乎？", literal: "Xiao He remonstrated, saying: “Though ruling Hanzhong is vile, is it not still better than death?", idiomatic: "Xiao He urged: “However bad ruling Hanzhong may be, is it not better than death?" },
  { zh: "」漢王曰：「何為乃死也？", literal: "” The King of Han said: “Why would it come to death?", idiomatic: "” The King of Han said, “Why should it mean death?" },
  { zh: "」何曰：「今眾弗如，百戰百敗，不死何為？", literal: "” He said: “Now our masses are not his equal; a hundred battles, a hundred defeats—if not death, what?", idiomatic: "” Xiao He said, “Our forces are weaker; fight a hundred times, lose a hundred times—if not death, what then?" },
  { zh: "夫能詘於一人之下而信於萬乘之上者，湯、武是也。", literal: "Those who can bend beneath one man yet be trusted above a chariot of ten thousand—Tang and Wu were such.", idiomatic: "To bow beneath one man yet win trust above ten thousand chariots—that was Tang and Wu." },
  { zh: "臣願大王王漢中，養其民以致賢人，收用巴、蜀，還定三秦，天下可圖也。", literal: "Your servant wishes the great king to be king in Hanzhong, nurture the people to attract worthy men, gather and employ Ba and Shu, return to settle the Three Qins—the empire may then be contended for.”", idiomatic: "I urge Your Majesty to take Hanzhong, nurture the people and draw worthies, hold Ba and Shu, then recover the Three Qins—the empire can still be won.”" },
  { zh: "」漢王曰：「善！", literal: "” The King of Han said: “Good!", idiomatic: "” The King of Han said, “Well said!" },
  { zh: "」乃遂就國，以何為丞相。", literal: "” He thereupon went to his state and made He chancellor.", idiomatic: "” He went to his kingdom and made Xiao He chancellor." },
  { zh: "漢王賜張良金百鎰，珠二斗；", literal: "The King of Han gave Zhang Liang a hundred yi of gold and two dou of pearls;", idiomatic: "The King of Han gave Zhang Liang a hundred yi of gold and two dou of pearls;" },
  { zh: "良具以獻項伯。", literal: "Liang fully prepared them and presented them to Xiang Bo.", idiomatic: "Liang had everything prepared and presented it to Xiang Bo." },
  { zh: "漢王亦因令良厚遺項伯，使盡請漢中地，項王許之。", literal: "The King of Han also thereupon ordered Liang to send Xiang Bo generous gifts, had him fully request the lands of Hanzhong, and the King of Xiang granted it.", idiomatic: "The King of Han also had Liang send Xiang Bo generous gifts and ask that all the Hanzhong territory be granted; the King of Xiang agreed." },
  { zh: "夏，四月，諸侯罷戲下兵，各就國。", literal: "In summer, the fourth month, the feudal lords dismissed the troops below the play, each returning to his state.", idiomatic: "In summer, the fourth month, the feudal lords dismissed their armies at Xià and each returned to his domain." },
  { zh: "項王使卒三萬人從漢王之國。", literal: "The King of Xiang sent thirty thousand soldiers to accompany the King of Han to his state.", idiomatic: "The King of Xiang sent thirty thousand men to escort the King of Han to his domain." },
  { zh: "楚與諸侯之慕從者數萬人，從杜南入蝕中。", literal: "Chu men and those of the feudal lords who admired and followed him numbered several tens of thousands; they entered Zhi from the south of Du.", idiomatic: "Several tens of thousands of Chu men and followers from the other lords entered Zhi from the south of Du." },
  { zh: "張良送至褒中，漢王遣良歸韓；", literal: "Zhang Liang escorted him to Baozhong; the King of Han sent Liang back to Han;", idiomatic: "Zhang Liang escorted him to Baozhong; the King of Han sent Liang back to Han;" },
  { zh: "良因說漢王燒絕所過棧道，以備諸侯盜兵，且示項羽無東意。", literal: "Liang thereupon urged the King of Han to burn and sever the plank roads they had passed, to guard against feudal lords’ raiding troops and also to show Xiang Yu that he had no intent to go east.", idiomatic: "Liang then urged the King of Han to burn the plank roads along their route, to guard against raids by other lords and to show Xiang Yu that he had no intention of marching east." },
  { zh: "5田榮聞項羽徙齊王市於膠東，而以田都為齊王，大怒。", literal: "5. Tian Rong heard that Xiang Yu had moved King Shi of Qi to Jiaodong and made Tian Du king of Qi, and was greatly enraged.", idiomatic: "5. When Tian Rong heard that Xiang Yu had moved King Shi of Qi to Jiaodong and made Tian Du king of Qi, he was furious." },
  { zh: "五月，榮發兵距擊田都，都亡走楚。", literal: "In the fifth month, Rong raised troops to block and strike Tian Du; Du fled and ran to Chu.", idiomatic: "In the fifth month, Rong raised troops to resist Tian Du; Du fled to Chu." },
  { zh: "榮留齊王市，不令之膠東。", literal: "Rong detained King Shi of Qi and would not let him go to Jiaodong.", idiomatic: "Rong detained King Shi of Qi and would not let him proceed to Jiaodong." },
  { zh: "市畏項羽，竊亡之國。", literal: "Shi feared Xiang Yu and secretly fled to his state.", idiomatic: "Shi, fearing Xiang Yu, secretly fled back to his domain." },
  { zh: "榮怒，六月，追擊殺市於即墨，自立為齊王。", literal: "Rong was enraged; in the sixth month he pursued, struck, and killed Shi at Jimo, and installed himself as king of Qi.", idiomatic: "Enraged, in the sixth month Rong pursued him, killed Shi at Jimo, and declared himself king of Qi." },
  { zh: "是時，彭越在巨野，有眾萬餘人，無所屬。", literal: "At this time Peng Yue was at Juye, had a host of more than ten thousand men, and belonged to no one.", idiomatic: "At this time Peng Yue was at Juye with more than ten thousand men and no lord to follow." },
  { zh: "榮與越將軍印，使擊濟北。", literal: "Rong gave Yue a general’s seal and had him attack Jibei.", idiomatic: "Rong gave Yue a general’s seal and sent him to attack Jibei." },
  { zh: "秋，七月，越擊殺濟北王安。", literal: "In autumn, the seventh month, Yue attacked and killed King An of Jibei.", idiomatic: "In autumn, the seventh month, Yue attacked and killed King An of Jibei." },
  { zh: "榮遂並王三齊之地，又使越擊楚。", literal: "Rong thereupon united and ruled the lands of the Three Qi, and again sent Yue to attack Chu.", idiomatic: "Rong then united the Three Qi domains and again sent Yue to attack Chu." },
  { zh: "項王命蕭公角將兵擊越，越大破楚軍。", literal: "The King of Xiang ordered Lord Jiao of Xiao to command troops against Yue; Yue greatly routed the Chu army.", idiomatic: "The King of Xiang ordered Lord Jiao of Xiao to attack Yue; Yue routed the Chu army." },
  { zh: "6張耳之國，陳餘益怒曰：「張耳與餘，功等也。", literal: "6. In Zhang Er’s state, Chen Yu grew ever angrier and said: “Zhang Er and Yu have equal merit.", idiomatic: "6. In Zhang Er’s domain, Chen Yu grew angrier and said: “Zhang Er and I have equal merit.”" },
  { zh: "今張耳王，餘獨侯，此項羽不平！", literal: "Now Zhang Er is king while Yu alone is a marquis—this is Xiang Yu’s unfairness!", idiomatic: "Now Zhang Er is king while I alone am a marquis—this is Xiang Yu’s injustice!”" },
  { zh: "」乃陰使張同、夏說說齊王榮曰：「項羽為天下宰不平，盡王諸將善地，徙故王於丑地。", literal: "” He thereupon secretly sent Zhang Tong and Xia Shuo to persuade King Rong of Qi, saying: “Xiang Yu as arbiter of All under Heaven is unfair: he has made all the generals kings in fine lands and moved the former kings to ugly lands.", idiomatic: "” He secretly sent Zhang Tong and Xia Shuo to persuade King Rong of Qi: “As arbiter of the realm Xiang Yu is unjust—he makes his generals kings in the best lands and moves the former kings to the worst.”" },
  { zh: "今趙王乃北居代，餘以為不可。", literal: "Now the King of Zhao is made to dwell north in Dai—Yu considers this unacceptable.", idiomatic: "Now the King of Zhao is forced to live north in Dai—I consider that unacceptable.”" },
  { zh: "聞大王起兵，不聽不義。", literal: "Hearing that the great king has raised troops, he will not heed what is unrighteous.", idiomatic: "Hearing that Your Majesty has raised troops, he will not heed what is unrighteous.”" },
  { zh: "願大王資餘兵擊常山，復趙王，請以趙為扞蔽！", literal: "I beg the great king to supply Yu with troops to attack Changshan, restore the King of Zhao, and let Zhao serve as a shield and barrier!", idiomatic: "I beg Your Majesty to supply me with troops to attack Changshan, restore the King of Zhao, and let Zhao serve as your shield!”" },
  { zh: "」齊王許之，遣兵從陳餘。", literal: "” The King of Qi agreed and sent troops to follow Chen Yu.", idiomatic: "” The King of Qi agreed and sent troops to follow Chen Yu." },
  { zh: "7項王以張良從漢王，韓王成又無功，故不遣之國，與俱至彭城，廢以為穰侯；", literal: "7. The King of Xiang, because Zhang Liang had followed the King of Han and King Cheng of Han had again achieved no merit, therefore did not send him to his state but went with him together to Pengcheng, deposed him and made him Marquis of Rang;", idiomatic: "7. Because Zhang Liang had followed the King of Han and King Cheng of Han had achieved no merit, the King of Xiang did not send him to his domain but took him to Pengcheng, deposed him, and made him Marquis of Rang;" },
  { zh: "已，又殺之。", literal: "afterward he again killed him.", idiomatic: "then killed him." },
  { zh: "8初，淮陰人韓信，家貧，無行，不得推擇為吏，又不能治生商賈，常從人寄食飲，人多厭之。", literal: "8. Initially, Han Xin of Huaiyin—his family was poor, his conduct base; he could not be recommended and selected as an official, nor could he manage livelihood through trade; he constantly relied on others for food and drink, and many people despised him.", idiomatic: "8. Initially, Han Xin of Huaiyin was from a poor family and of base conduct; he could not be recommended for office nor make a living in trade, and often ate at others’ tables—many despised him." },
  { zh: "信釣於城下，有漂母見信饑，飯信。", literal: "Xin was fishing below the city wall; a woman who bleached cloth saw Xin hungry and fed Xin.", idiomatic: "Xin was fishing by the city wall when a washerwoman saw him hungry and fed him." },
  { zh: "信喜，謂漂母曰：「吾必有以重報母。", literal: "Xin was pleased and said to the washerwoman: “I shall surely have means to repay you heavily, mother.", idiomatic: "Xin was pleased and said to her: “I shall surely repay you generously, mother.”" },
  { zh: "」母怒曰：「大丈夫不能自食，吾哀王孫而進食，豈望報乎？", literal: "” The woman angrily said: “A great man who cannot feed himself—I pitied the young lord and gave him food; how could I expect repayment?", idiomatic: "” She snapped: “A grown man who cannot feed himself—I pitied you and gave you food; did I expect repayment?”" },
  { zh: "」淮陰屠中少年有侮信者曰：「若雖長大，好帶刀劍，中情怯耳。", literal: "” Among the butcher youths of Huaiyin was one who insulted Xin, saying: “Though you are grown tall and love to wear sword and blade, at heart you are timid.", idiomatic: "” A butcher’s lad who bullied Xin said: “Though you are tall and fond of wearing a sword, at heart you are a coward.”" },
  { zh: "」因眾辱之曰：「信能死，刺我；", literal: "” He thereupon before the crowd shamed him, saying: “If Xin can die, stab me;", idiomatic: "” Before the crowd he mocked him: “If you have the nerve to die, stab me;" },
  { zh: "不能死，出我胯下！", literal: "if you cannot die, come out from under my crotch!", idiomatic: "if not, crawl between my legs!”" },
  { zh: "」於是信孰視之，俛出胯下，蒲伏。", literal: "” Thereupon Xin stared fixedly at him, bent and came out from under his crotch, crawling prostrate.", idiomatic: "” Xin stared at him, then bent low and crawled between his legs." },
  { zh: "一市人皆笑信，以為怯。", literal: "Everyone in the market laughed at Xin and thought him timid.", idiomatic: "The whole market laughed at Xin and thought him a coward." },
  { zh: "及項梁渡淮，信杖劍從之。", literal: "When Xiang Liang crossed the Huai, Xin leaned on his sword and followed him.", idiomatic: "When Xiang Liang crossed the Huai, Xin took sword in hand and followed him." },
  { zh: "居麾下，無所知名。", literal: "He dwelt under his banner and was known nowhere.", idiomatic: "He served under his banner and remained unknown." },
  { zh: "項梁敗，又屬項羽，羽以為郎中。", literal: "When Xiang Liang was defeated, he again attached himself to Xiang Yu; Yu made him a palace attendant.", idiomatic: "After Xiang Liang’s defeat he joined Xiang Yu, who made him a palace attendant." },
  { zh: "數以策干羽，羽不用。", literal: "Several times he offered stratagems to seek favor with Yu; Yu did not employ him.", idiomatic: "Several times he offered plans to Yu; Yu ignored them." },
  { zh: "漢王之入蜀，信亡楚歸漢，未知名。", literal: "When the King of Han entered Shu, Xin fled Chu and returned to Han, still unknown.", idiomatic: "When the King of Han entered Shu, Xin fled Chu for Han and was still unknown." },
  { zh: "為連敖，坐當斬。", literal: "He served as a senior camp officer and sat in judgment for an offense warranting beheading.", idiomatic: "He was made a senior camp officer and was sentenced to beheading." },
  { zh: "其輩十三人皆已斬，次至信，信乃仰視，適見滕公，曰：「上不欲就天下乎？", literal: "His companions, thirteen men, had all already been beheaded; when it came to Xin’s turn, Xin raised his head and looked up, just then seeing the Lord of Teng, and said: “Does not the sovereign wish to gain All under Heaven?", idiomatic: "His thirteen companions had already been executed; when his turn came, Xin looked up, saw the Lord of Teng, and said: “Does Your Majesty not wish to gain the realm?”" },
  { zh: "何為斬壯士？", literal: "Why behead a stalwart?", idiomatic: "Why behead a stalwart?”" },
  { zh: "」滕公奇其言，壯其貌，釋而不斬。", literal: "” The Lord of Teng marveled at his words and esteemed his appearance; he released him and did not behead him.", idiomatic: "” The Lord of Teng marveled at his words and was struck by his bearing; he released him and did not execute him." },
  { zh: "與語，大說之，言於王。", literal: "He conversed with him, was greatly pleased with him, and spoke of him to the king.", idiomatic: "He spoke with him, was greatly pleased, and reported him to the king." },
  { zh: "王拜以為治粟都尉，亦未之奇也。", literal: "The king appointed him Director of Grain but also did not regard him as extraordinary.", idiomatic: "The king appointed him Director of Grain but still did not regard him as extraordinary." },
  { zh: "信數與蕭何語，何奇之。", literal: "Xin several times conversed with Xiao He; He marveled at him.", idiomatic: "Xin often spoke with Xiao He, who was struck by his talent." },
  { zh: "漢王至南鄭，諸將及士卒皆歌謳思東歸，多道亡者。", literal: "When the King of Han reached Nanzheng, the generals and soldiers all sang songs longing to return east; many fled along the roads.", idiomatic: "When the King of Han reached Nanzheng, officers and men sang songs of longing to return east, and many deserted along the way." },
  { zh: "信度何等已數言王，王不我用，即亡去。", literal: "Xin reckoned that He and the rest had already several times spoken to the king, yet the king did not employ him—he would at once flee and leave.", idiomatic: "Xin reckoned that He had already spoken for him several times yet the king would not employ him, and prepared to flee." },
  { zh: "何聞信亡，不及以聞，自追之。", literal: "He, hearing that Xin had fled, had no time to report it and pursued him himself.", idiomatic: "When He heard that Xin had fled, he had no time to report it and pursued him himself." },
  { zh: "人有言王曰：「丞相何亡。", literal: "Someone told the king: “Chancellor He has fled.", idiomatic: "Someone told the king: “Chancellor He has fled.”" },
  { zh: "」王大怒，如失左右手。", literal: "” The king was greatly enraged, as if he had lost his left and right hands.", idiomatic: "” The king was furious, as if he had lost both hands." },
  { zh: "居一二日，何來謁王。", literal: "After a day or two, He came to audience with the king.", idiomatic: "A day or two later, He came to see the king." },
  { zh: "王且怒且喜，罵何曰：「若亡，何也？", literal: "The king was both angry and pleased and cursed He, saying: “You fled—why?", idiomatic: "The king was angry yet relieved and cursed him: “You fled—why?”" },
  { zh: "」何曰：「臣不敢亡也，臣追亡者耳。", literal: "” He said: “Your servant did not dare flee; your servant was pursuing one who had fled.", idiomatic: "” He said: “I did not flee; I was pursuing a deserter.”" },
  { zh: "」王曰：「若所追者誰？", literal: "” The king said: “Whom did you pursue?", idiomatic: "” The king asked: “Whom did you pursue?”" },
  { zh: "」何曰：「韓信也。", literal: "” He said: “Han Xin.", idiomatic: "” He said: “Han Xin.”" },
  { zh: "」王復罵曰：「諸將亡者以十數，公無所追。", literal: "” The king cursed again: “Generals who have fled number in the tens; you pursued none of them.", idiomatic: "” The king cursed again: “Dozens of generals have deserted and you pursued none of them.”" },
  { zh: "追信，詐也。", literal: "To pursue Xin is deception.", idiomatic: "Pursuing Xin is a lie.”" },
  { zh: "」何曰：「諸將易得耳。", literal: "” He said: “The generals are easily obtained.", idiomatic: "” He said: “Generals are easily replaced.”" },
  { zh: "至如信者，國士無雙。", literal: "As for one like Xin, there is no second such state-worthy man.", idiomatic: "But one like Xin is matchless in the realm.”" },
  { zh: "王必欲長王漢中，無所事信，必欲爭天下，非信無可與計事者。", literal: "If the king must wish to long rule Hanzhong, there is no need to employ Xin; if the king must wish to contend for All under Heaven, apart from Xin there is no one with whom to plan affairs.", idiomatic: "If Your Majesty wishes only to hold Hanzhong, you need not use Xin; if you wish to contend for the realm, apart from Xin there is no one with whom to plan.”" },
  { zh: "顧王策安所決耳。", literal: "Only look—where does the king’s strategy decide?", idiomatic: "It depends on which course Your Majesty chooses.”" },
  { zh: "」王曰：「吾亦欲東耳，安能鬱鬱久居此乎？", literal: "” The king said: “I too wish to go east—how could I dwell here in dejection long?", idiomatic: "” The king said: “I too wish to go east—how could I stay here in dejection?”" },
  { zh: "」何曰：「計必欲東，能用信，信即留；", literal: "” He said: “If the plan must be to go east, if you can employ Xin, Xin will stay;", idiomatic: "” He said: “If you are resolved to go east, employ Xin and he will stay;" },
  { zh: "不能用信，終亡耳。", literal: "if you cannot employ Xin, in the end he will flee.", idiomatic: "if you cannot employ him, in the end he will leave.”" },
  { zh: "」王曰：「吾為公以為將。", literal: "” The king said: “For your sake I will make him a general.", idiomatic: "” The king said: “For your sake I will make him a general.”" },
  { zh: "」何曰：「雖為將，信不留。", literal: "” He said: “Though made a general, Xin will not stay.", idiomatic: "” He said: “Even as a general, Xin will not stay.”" },
  { zh: "」王曰：「以為大將。", literal: "” The king said: “Make him grand commander.", idiomatic: "” The king said: “Make him grand commander.”" },
  { zh: "」何曰：「幸甚！", literal: "” He said: “Excellent!", idiomatic: "” He said: “Excellent!”" },
  { zh: "」於是王欲召信拜之。", literal: "” Thereupon the king wished to summon Xin and appoint him.", idiomatic: "” The king then wished to summon Xin and appoint him." },
  { zh: "何曰：「王素慢無禮。", literal: "He said: “The king has always been negligent and without ceremony.", idiomatic: "He said: “Your Majesty has always been casual and discourteous.”" },
  { zh: "今拜大將，如呼小兒，此乃信所以去也。", literal: "Now to appoint the grand commander like calling a child—this is why Xin left.", idiomatic: "To appoint a grand commander as you would summon a child—that is why Xin left.”" },
  { zh: "王必欲拜之，擇良日，齋戒，設壇場，具禮，乃可耳。", literal: "If the king must wish to appoint him, choose an auspicious day, fast and purify, set up an altar platform, complete the rites—only then may it be done.", idiomatic: "If you truly wish to appoint him, choose an auspicious day, fast, set up an altar, and perform the full rites—only then will it suffice.”" },
  { zh: "」王許之。", literal: "” The king agreed.", idiomatic: "” The king agreed." },
  { zh: "諸將皆喜，人人各自以為得大將。", literal: "The generals were all pleased; each thought he himself would obtain the post of grand commander.", idiomatic: "The generals were pleased; each thought he would be named grand commander." },
  { zh: "至拜大將，乃韓信也，一軍皆驚。", literal: "When the grand commander was appointed, it was Han Xin—the whole army was startled.", idiomatic: "When the grand commander was appointed, it was Han Xin, and the whole army was astonished." },
  { zh: "信拜禮畢，上坐。", literal: "When Xin’s bowing ceremony was finished, he ascended and sat.", idiomatic: "When the ceremony of appointment was finished, Xin took his seat." },
  { zh: "王曰：「丞相數言將軍，將軍何以教寡人計策？", literal: "The king said: “The chancellor has several times spoken of the general—by what stratagems will the general teach me, the few?", idiomatic: "The king said: “The chancellor has spoken of you often—what plans will you teach me?”" },
  { zh: "」信辭謝，因問王曰：「今東鄉爭權天下，豈非項王耶？", literal: "” Xin declined with thanks and thereupon asked the king: “Now in contending for power in All under Heaven facing east, is it not the King of Xiang?", idiomatic: "” Xin declined politely and asked: “In contending for the realm facing east today, is not your rival the King of Xiang?”" },
  { zh: "」漢王曰：「然。", literal: "” The King of Han said: “Yes.", idiomatic: "” The King of Han said: “Yes.”" },
  { zh: "」曰：「大王自料勇悍仁強孰與項王？", literal: "” He said: “Great King, judging for yourself—courage, fierceness, benevolence, and strength—which compares with the King of Xiang?", idiomatic: "” He said: “Which do you judge the stronger—yourself or the King of Xiang—in courage, fierceness, benevolence, and strength?”" },
  { zh: "」漢王默然良久，曰：「不如也。", literal: "” The King of Han was silent a long while and said: “I am not his equal.", idiomatic: "” The King of Han was silent a long while and said: “I am not his equal.”" },
  { zh: "」信再拜賀曰：「惟信亦以為大王不如也。", literal: "” Xin bowed again in congratulation and said: “Only Xin too considers that the great king is not his equal.", idiomatic: "” Xin bowed again and said: “I too believe Your Majesty is not his equal.”" },
  { zh: "然臣嘗事之，請言項王之為人也。", literal: "Yet your servant once served him; allow me to speak of the King of Xiang’s conduct as a man.", idiomatic: "Yet I once served him; let me describe the King of Xiang’s character.”" },
  { zh: "項王暗噁叱吒，千人皆廢，然不能任屬賢將，此特匹夫之勇耳。", literal: "The King of Xiang with scowl and shout could make a thousand men collapse, yet he cannot entrust and employ worthy generals—this is merely the courage of a common fellow.", idiomatic: "The King of Xiang with a glare and shout can terrify a thousand men, yet he cannot entrust command to worthy generals—this is merely the courage of a common brawler.”" },
  { zh: "項王見人，恭敬慈愛，言語嘔嘔，人有疾病，涕泣分食飲；", literal: "The King of Xiang, seeing people, was respectful and kindly loving; his speech was gentle and kind; when someone was ill he wept and shared food and drink;", idiomatic: "The King of Xiang is respectful and kindly in person, gentle in speech, and when someone is ill he weeps and shares his food;" },
  { zh: "至使人，有功當封爵者，印刓敝，忍不能予，此所謂婦人之仁也。", literal: "yet when he sends men forth, for those with merit who ought to receive enfeoffment, the seal is worn and damaged and he begrudges and cannot give—this is what is called a woman’s benevolence.", idiomatic: "yet when men deserve enfeoffment for merit, his seals are worn smooth and he cannot bear to grant them—this is what is called a woman’s kindness.”" },
  { zh: "項王雖霸天下而臣諸侯，不居關中而都彭城；", literal: "The King of Xiang, though he hegemonized All under Heaven and made the feudal lords his ministers, did not dwell in Guanzhong but made Pengcheng his capital;", idiomatic: "Though the King of Xiang hegemonized the realm and made the lords his ministers, he did not hold Guanzhong but made Pengcheng his capital;" },
  { zh: "背義帝之約，而以親愛王諸侯，不平；", literal: "he turned his back on the agreement with Emperor Yi and made the feudal lords kings according to his favorites—unfair;", idiomatic: "he broke his pact with Emperor Yi and enfeoffed lords by favoritism—unjust;" },
  { zh: "逐其故主而王其將相，又遷逐義帝置江南；", literal: "he drove off their former lords and made his generals and chancellors kings, and again moved and drove Emperor Yi to set him in the lands south of the Yangtze;", idiomatic: "he drove out former kings and made his own generals and ministers kings, and banished Emperor Yi to the south;" },
  { zh: "所過無不殘滅，百姓不親附，特劫於威強耳。", literal: "wherever he passed there was nothing not laid waste and destroyed; the common people did not attach themselves to him—they were only coerced by might and strength.", idiomatic: "wherever he marched he laid waste; the people do not love him—they submit only to his might.”" },
  { zh: "名雖為霸，實失天下心，故其強易弱。", literal: "His name though hegemon, in reality he has lost the hearts of All under Heaven; therefore his strength is easily made weak.", idiomatic: "Though called hegemon, he has lost the hearts of the realm; his strength can easily be broken.”" },
  { zh: "今大王誠能反其道，任天下武勇，何所不誅以？", literal: "Now if the great king can truly reverse his way, employ the martial valor of All under Heaven—what would not be destroyed?", idiomatic: "If Your Majesty can truly reverse his course and employ the brave of the realm, what enemy could you not destroy?”" },
  { zh: "天下城邑封功臣，何所不服？", literal: "Enfeoff meritorious ministers with the cities and towns of All under Heaven—who would not submit?", idiomatic: "Enfeoff your meritorious men with the cities of the realm—who would not submit?”" },
  { zh: "以義兵從思東歸之士，何所不散？", literal: "With righteous troops follow soldiers who long to return east—what would not be scattered?", idiomatic: "Lead righteous troops with men who long to return east—what foe could stand?”" },
  { zh: "且三秦王為秦將，將秦子弟數歲矣，所殺亡不可勝計；", literal: "Moreover, the Three Kings of Qin were Qin generals who led Qin’s young men for several years; those they killed and destroyed cannot be counted;", idiomatic: "Moreover, the Three Kings of Qin were Qin generals who led Qin’s sons for years and killed untold numbers;" },
  { zh: "又欺其眾降諸侯，至新安，項王詐坑秦降卒二十餘萬，唯獨邯、欣、翳得脫。", literal: "again they deceived their hosts in surrendering to the feudal lords; at Xin’an the King of Xiang by fraud buried alive more than two hundred thousand Qin surrendered soldiers—only Zhang Han, Sima Xin, and Dong Yi escaped.", idiomatic: "they deceived their men into surrendering to the lords; at Xin’an the King of Xiang treacherously buried alive more than two hundred thousand surrendered Qin soldiers—only Zhang Han, Sima Xin, and Dong Yi escaped.”" },
  { zh: "秦父兄怨此三人，痛入骨髓。", literal: "The fathers and elder brothers of Qin hate these three men; the pain enters to the marrow.", idiomatic: "The elders of Qin hate these three men to the marrow.”" },
  { zh: "今楚強以威王此三人，秦民莫愛也。", literal: "Now Chu by might makes these three kings; the people of Qin love none of them.", idiomatic: "Now Chu by force makes them kings, and the people of Qin love none of them." },
  { zh: "大王之入武關，秋毫無所害；", literal: "When the Great King entered Wu Pass, not a hair's breadth of harm was done;", idiomatic: "When Your Majesty entered Wu Pass, not the slightest harm was done;" },
  { zh: "除秦苛法，與秦民約法三章；", literal: "the harsh laws of Qin were abolished and a three-article compact was made with the people of Qin;", idiomatic: "you abolished Qin's harsh laws and pledged the three articles of law to the Qin people;" },
  { zh: "秦民無不欲得大王王秦者。", literal: "among the people of Qin there was none who did not wish to have the Great King made king of Qin.", idiomatic: "every man in Qin wished to see you made king of Qin." },
  { zh: "於諸侯之約，大王當王關中，民鹹知之；", literal: "Under the covenant among the allies, the Great King was to be king in Guanzhong, and the people all knew it;", idiomatic: "by the covenant among the allies you were to be king in Guanzhong, and the people all knew it;" },
  { zh: "大王失職入漢中，秦民無不恨者。", literal: "when the Great King lost his post and entered Hanzhong, among the people of Qin there was none who did not resent it.", idiomatic: "when you were displaced into Hanzhong, every Qin man resented it." },
  { zh: "今大王舉而東，三秦可傳檄而定也。", literal: "Now if the Great King raises his standard and goes east, the Three Qins can be settled by passing down a proclamation alone.", idiomatic: "Now if you march east, the Three Qins can be won by proclamation alone." },
  { zh: "」於是漢王大喜，自以為得信晚，遂聽信計，部署諸將所擊。", literal: "” Thereupon the King of Han was greatly pleased, thought himself late in gaining Xin, followed Xin's plan, and assigned each general his target.", idiomatic: "” The King of Han was overjoyed, regretted only that he had found Xin so late, adopted his plan, and assigned each general his objective." },
  { zh: "留蕭何收巴、蜀租，給軍糧食。", literal: "He left Xiao He to collect the rents of Ba and Shu and supply the army with grain.", idiomatic: "He left Xiao He to gather rents from Ba and Shu and provision the army." },
  { zh: "9八月，漢王引兵從故道出，襲雍；", literal: "9 In the eighth month, the King of Han led his army out by the old road and struck Yong;", idiomatic: "9 In the eighth month, the King of Han marched out by the old road and surprised Yong;" },
  { zh: "雍王章邯迎擊漢陳倉。", literal: "the King of Yong, Zhang Han, met him in battle at Chencang on the Han side.", idiomatic: "the King of Yong, Zhang Han, met him at Chencang." },
  { zh: "雍兵敗，還走；", literal: "The Yong army was defeated and retreated;", idiomatic: "The Yong army was beaten and fell back;" },
  { zh: "止，戰好畤，又敗，走廢丘。", literal: "halting, they fought at Haozhi, were defeated again, and fled to Feiqiu.", idiomatic: "they halted to fight at Haozhi, were beaten again, and fled to Feiqiu." },
  { zh: "漢王遂定雍地，東至咸陽，引兵圍雍王於廢丘，而遣諸將略地。", literal: "The King of Han thereupon settled the territory of Yong, advanced east to Xianyang, led troops to besiege the King of Yong at Feiqiu, and sent the various generals to seize territory.", idiomatic: "The King of Han then secured Yong, reached Xianyang in the east, besieged the King of Yong at Feiqiu, and sent his generals to overrun the countryside." },
  { zh: "塞王欣、翟王翳皆降，以其地為渭南、河上、上郡。", literal: "the King of Sai, Sima Xin, and the King of Di, Dong Yi, both surrendered; their lands were made Weinan, Heshang, and Shang commanderies.", idiomatic: "the Kings of Sai and Di, Sima Xin and Dong Yi, both surrendered; their territories became Weinan, Heshang, and Shang commanderies." },
  { zh: "將軍薛歐、王吸出武關，因王陵兵以迎太公、呂后。", literal: "Generals Xue Ou and Wang Xi went out through Wu Pass and, relying on Wang Ling's troops, went to receive the Grand Duke and Empress Lü.", idiomatic: "Generals Xue Ou and Wang Xi marched out through Wu Pass and, with Wang Ling's force, went to fetch the Grand Duke and Empress Lü." },
  { zh: "項王聞之，發兵距之陽夏，不得前。", literal: "the King of Xiang heard of it, sent troops to block them at Yangxia, and they could not advance.", idiomatic: "the King of Xiang heard of it, sent troops to block them at Yangxia, and they could not get through." },
  { zh: "王陵者，沛人也，先聚黨數千人，居南陽，至是始以兵屬漢。", literal: "Wang Ling was a man of Pei who had first gathered a band of several thousand men and dwelt in Nanyang; only now did he first submit his troops to Han.", idiomatic: "Wang Ling was from Pei; he had first gathered several thousand followers and held Nanyang, and only now brought his force under Han." },
  { zh: "項王取陵母置軍中，陵使至，則東鄉坐陵母，欲以招陵。", literal: "the King of Xiang took Ling's mother and placed her in the army; when Ling's envoy arrived, he seated Ling's mother facing east, wishing thereby to win Ling over.", idiomatic: "the King of Xiang seized Ling's mother and kept her in camp; when Ling's envoy came, he seated her facing east to lure Ling back." },
  { zh: "陵母私送使者，泣曰：「願為老妾語陵：善事漢王，漢王長者，終得天下，毋以老妾故持二心。", literal: "Ling's mother secretly sent off the envoy and, weeping, said, “I wish to speak to Ling for this old woman: serve the King of Han well. The King of Han is a man of virtue and will in the end gain the realm—do not hold two hearts on account of this old woman.", idiomatic: "Ling's mother secretly sent the envoy away and wept: “Tell Ling for me: serve the King of Han well. He is a man of virtue and will win the realm in the end—do not waver on my account." },
  { zh: "妾以死送使者！", literal: "This old woman dies to send off the envoy!", idiomatic: "I die to send you off!" },
  { zh: "」遂伏劍而死。", literal: "” She then fell on her sword and died.", idiomatic: "” She then fell on her sword and died." },
  { zh: "項王怒。", literal: "The King of Xiang was enraged.", idiomatic: "The King of Xiang was furious." },
  { zh: "烹陵母。", literal: "He boiled Ling's mother.", idiomatic: "He had Ling's mother boiled alive." },
  { zh: "項王以故吳令鄭昌為韓王，以距漢。", literal: "The King of Xiang made the former magistrate of Wu, Zheng Chang, King of Han to block Han.", idiomatic: "The King of Xiang made the former Wu magistrate Zheng Chang King of Han to hold back Han." },
  { zh: "張良遺項王書曰：「漢王失職，欲得關中，如約即止，不敢東。", literal: "Zhang Liang sent the King of Xiang a letter saying, “The King of Han lost his post and wishes to have Guanzhong; if the covenant is fulfilled he will stop and not dare go east.", idiomatic: "Zhang Liang sent the King of Xiang a letter: “The King of Han was displaced and wants Guanzhong back; once the covenant is honored he will stop and not march east." },
  { zh: "」又以齊、梁反書遺項王曰：「齊欲與趙並滅楚。", literal: "” He also sent the King of Xiang a letter of rebellion from Qi and Liang, saying, “Qi wishes to join Zhao in destroying Chu together.", idiomatic: "” He also sent a forged letter from Qi and Liang saying, “Qi intends to join Zhao in destroying Chu." },
  { zh: "」項王以此故無西意，而北擊齊。", literal: "” For this reason the King of Xiang had no mind to go west and instead marched north to attack Qi.", idiomatic: "” For this reason the King of Xiang gave up any thought of going west and marched north against Qi." },
  { zh: "10燕王廣不肯之遼東，臧荼擊殺之，並其地。", literal: "10 The King of Yan, Guang, refused to go to Liaodong; Zang Tu attacked and killed him and annexed his territory.", idiomatic: "10 The King of Yan, Guang, refused to go to Liaodong; Zang Tu attacked and killed him and took his lands." },
  { zh: "11是歲，以內史沛周苛為御史大夫。", literal: "11 That year, Zhou Ke of Pei, inner scribe, was made grand censor.", idiomatic: "11 That year Zhou Ke of Pei, the metropolitan administrator, was appointed grand censor." },
  { zh: "12項王使趣義帝行，其群臣、左右稍稍叛之。", literal: "12 The King of Xiang urged the Emperor Yi to move on his way; his ministers and attendants little by little deserted him.", idiomatic: "12 The King of Xiang pressed Emperor Yi to move on; his ministers and attendants gradually deserted him." },
  { zh: "1冬，十月，項王密使九江、衡山、臨江王擊義帝，殺之江中。", literal: "1 In winter, the tenth month, the King of Xiang secretly sent the kings of Jiujiang, Hengshan, and Linjiang to strike the Emperor Yi and killed him in the river.", idiomatic: "1 In winter, the tenth month, the King of Xiang secretly sent the kings of Jiujiang, Hengshan, and Linjiang against Emperor Yi and had him killed in the Yangtze." },
  { zh: "2陳餘悉三縣兵，與齊兵共襲常山。", literal: "2 Chen Yu mustered the troops of three counties and, with Qi troops, jointly attacked Changshan.", idiomatic: "2 Chen Yu raised the troops of three counties and, with Qi, jointly attacked Changshan." },
  { zh: "常山王張耳敗，走漢，謁漢王於廢丘，漢王厚遇之。", literal: "the King of Changshan, Zhang Er, was defeated, fled to Han, and had audience with the King of Han at Feiqiu; the King of Han treated him generously.", idiomatic: "the King of Changshan, Zhang Er, was defeated, fled to Han, and met the King of Han at Feiqiu, who received him with great favor." },
  { zh: "陳餘迎趙王於代，復為趙王。", literal: "Chen Yu welcomed the King of Zhao from Dai and restored him as King of Zhao.", idiomatic: "Chen Yu brought the King of Zhao back from Dai and restored him to the throne." },
  { zh: "趙王德陳餘，立以為代王。", literal: "The King of Zhao was grateful to Chen Yu and established him as King of Dai.", idiomatic: "The King of Zhao, grateful to Chen Yu, made him King of Dai." },
  { zh: "陳餘為趙王弱，國初定，不之國，留傅趙王；", literal: "Chen Yu, considering the King of Zhao young and the state newly settled, did not go to his kingdom but stayed to tutor the King of Zhao;", idiomatic: "Chen Yu judged the King of Zhao too young and the state too newly settled to leave; he stayed to tutor the king;" },
  { zh: "而使夏說以相國守代。", literal: "and sent Xia Yue as chancellor to hold Dai.", idiomatic: "and sent Xia Yue as chancellor to hold Dai." },
  { zh: "3張良自韓間行歸漢，漢王以為成信侯。", literal: "3 Zhang Liang returned to Han by secret route from Han and was made Marquis of Chengxin.", idiomatic: "3 Zhang Liang slipped back to Han from Han territory by a secret route and was made Marquis of Chengxin." },
  { zh: "良多病，未嘗特將，常為畫策臣，時時從漢王。", literal: "Liang was often ill, had never commanded an army on his own, and regularly served as a planning adviser, sometimes accompanying the King of Han.", idiomatic: "Liang was often ill, never held independent command, and regularly served as strategist, sometimes accompanying the king." },
  { zh: "4漢王如陝，鎮撫關外父老。", literal: "4 The King of Han went to Shan and pacified and comforted the elders beyond the passes.", idiomatic: "4 The King of Han went to Shan to reassure the elders east of the passes." },
  { zh: "5河南王申陽降，置河南郡。", literal: "5 The King of Henan, Shen Yang, surrendered; Henan commandery was established.", idiomatic: "5 The King of Henan, Shen Yang, surrendered and his territory was made Henan commandery." },
  { zh: "6漢王以韓襄王孫信為韓太尉，將兵略韓地。", literal: "6 The King of Han made Sun Xin, grandson of King Xiang of Han, Grand Commandant of Han and sent him with troops to overrun Han territory.", idiomatic: "6 The King of Han made Sun Xin, grandson of King Xiang of Han, Grand Commandant of Han and sent him to overrun Han territory." },
  { zh: "信急擊韓王昌於陽城，昌降。", literal: "Xin pressed the attack on the King of Han, Chang, at Yangcheng; Chang surrendered.", idiomatic: "Xin pressed King Chang of Han at Yangcheng until he surrendered." },
  { zh: "十一月，立信為韓王，常將韓兵從漢王。", literal: "In the eleventh month Xin was established as King of Han and regularly led Han troops in attendance on the King of Han.", idiomatic: "In the eleventh month Xin was made King of Han and regularly led Han troops with the King of Han." },
  { zh: "7漢王還都櫟陽。", literal: "7 The King of Han returned and made his capital at Liyang.", idiomatic: "7 The King of Han returned and established his capital at Liyang." },
  { zh: "8諸將拔隴西。", literal: "8 The generals took Longxi.", idiomatic: "8 The generals captured Longxi." },
  { zh: "9春，正月，項王北至城陽。", literal: "9 In spring, the first month, the King of Xiang went north to Chengyang.", idiomatic: "9 In spring, the first month, the King of Xiang marched north to Chengyang." },
  { zh: "齊王榮將兵會戰，敗，走平原，平原民殺之。", literal: "the King of Qi, Rong, led his troops to join battle, was defeated, fled to Pingyuan, and the people of Pingyuan killed him.", idiomatic: "the King of Qi, Rong, met him in battle, was defeated, fled to Pingyuan, and the people there killed him." },
  { zh: "項王復立田假為齊王。", literal: "The King of Xiang again established Tian Jia as King of Qi.", idiomatic: "The King of Xiang reinstalled Tian Jia as King of Qi." },
  { zh: "遂北至北海，燒夷城郭、室屋，坑田榮降卒，系虜其老弱、婦女，所過多所殘滅。", literal: "He then went north to the sea, burned and leveled city walls and houses, buried alive Tian Rong's surrendered soldiers, bound and took captive the old, weak, and women, and wherever he passed left much destruction.", idiomatic: "He then marched north to the sea, burned towns and houses, buried Tian Rong's surrendered troops alive, bound up the old, weak, and women as captives, and left devastation wherever he passed." },
  { zh: "齊民相聚叛之。", literal: "The people of Qi gathered together and rebelled against him.", idiomatic: "The people of Qi rose everywhere in revolt against him." },
  { zh: "10漢將拔北地，虜雍王弟平。", literal: "10 Han generals took Beidi and captured Ping, younger brother of the King of Yong.", idiomatic: "10 Han generals took Beidi and captured Ping, the King of Yong's younger brother." },
  { zh: "11三月，漢王自臨晉渡河。", literal: "11 In the third month the King of Han crossed the river from Linjin.", idiomatic: "11 In the third month the King of Han crossed the Yellow River from Linjin." },
  { zh: "魏王豹降，將兵從；", literal: "the King of Wei, Bao, surrendered and led his troops to follow;", idiomatic: "the King of Wei, Bao, surrendered and followed with his troops;" },
  { zh: "下河內，虜殷王卬，置河內郡。", literal: "he descended on Henei, captured the King of Yin, Ang, and established Henei commandery.", idiomatic: "he took Henei, captured the King of Yin, Ang, and made it Henei commandery." },
  { zh: "12初，陽武人陳平，家貧，好讀書。", literal: "12 At first, Chen Ping of Yangwu, though his family was poor, loved reading.", idiomatic: "12 Earlier, Chen Ping of Yangwu was poor but loved books." },
  { zh: "里中社，平為宰，分肉食甚均。", literal: "At the community sacrifice in his ward, Ping served as steward and divided the meat very evenly.", idiomatic: "At the ward sacrifice Ping served as steward and divided the meat with perfect fairness." },
  { zh: "父老曰：「善，陳孺子之為宰！", literal: "The elders said, “Well done—Young Chen as steward!", idiomatic: "The elders said, “Well done, Young Chen as steward!" },
  { zh: "」平曰：「嗟乎，使平得宰天下，亦如是肉矣！", literal: "” Ping said, “Alas, if Ping could steward all under Heaven, it would be just like this meat!", idiomatic: "” Ping said, “Ah—if I could govern all under Heaven, I would divide it just as evenly as this meat!" },
  { zh: "」及諸侯叛秦，平事魏王咎於臨濟，為太僕，說魏王，不聽。", literal: "” When the allies rebelled against Qin, Ping served King Jia of Wei at Linji as grand steward; he urged the King of Wei, who would not listen.", idiomatic: "” When the allies rebelled against Qin, Ping served King Jia of Wei at Linji as grand steward; he remonstrated with the king, who would not listen." },
  { zh: "人或讒之，平亡去。", literal: "Someone slandered him and Ping fled.", idiomatic: "Someone slandered him and he fled." },
  { zh: "後事項羽，賜爵為卿。", literal: "Later he served Xiang Yu and was granted rank as minister.", idiomatic: "Later he served Xiang Yu and was ennobled as minister." },
  { zh: "殷王反楚，項羽使平擊降之。", literal: "When the King of Yin rebelled against Chu, Xiang Yu sent Ping to attack and subdue him.", idiomatic: "When the King of Yin rebelled against Chu, Xiang Yu sent Ping to crush him." },
  { zh: "還，拜為都尉，賜金二十鎰。", literal: "On his return he was appointed commandant and given twenty yi of gold.", idiomatic: "On his return he was made commandant and given twenty yi of gold." },
  { zh: "居無何，漢王攻下殷。", literal: "Before long the King of Han attacked and took Yin.", idiomatic: "Before long the King of Han captured Yin." },
  { zh: "項王怒，將誅定殷將吏。", literal: "The King of Xiang was enraged and was about to execute the Yin officers who had pacified Yin.", idiomatic: "The King of Xiang was furious and was about to execute the Yin officers who had held the region." },
  { zh: "平懼，乃封其金與印，使使歸項王；", literal: "Ping was afraid; he sealed up his gold and seal, sent an envoy to return them to the King of Xiang;", idiomatic: "Ping was afraid; he sealed up his gold and seal and sent them back to the King of Xiang;" },
  { zh: "而挺身間行，杖劍亡，渡河，歸漢王於脩武，因魏無知求見漢王。", literal: "and himself went by secret route, sword in hand, fled, crossed the river, and rejoined the King of Han at Xiuyang; through Wei Wuzhi he sought audience.", idiomatic: "then slipped away alone with sword in hand, crossed the river, joined the King of Han at Xiuyang, and through Wei Wuzhi asked for an audience." },
  { zh: "漢王召入，賜食，遣罷就舍。", literal: "The King of Han summoned him in, gave him food, and sent him off to his lodging.", idiomatic: "The King of Han received him, gave him a meal, and sent him to his quarters." },
  { zh: "平曰：「臣為事來，所言不可以過今日。", literal: "Ping said, “Your servant came on business; what is to be said cannot wait beyond today.", idiomatic: "Ping said, “I came on urgent business; what I have to say cannot wait until tomorrow." },
  { zh: "」於是漢王與語而說之。", literal: "” The King of Han then spoke with him and was pleased.", idiomatic: "” The king talked with him and was delighted." },
  { zh: "問曰：「子之居楚何官？", literal: "He asked, “What office did you hold in Chu?", idiomatic: "He asked, “What office did you hold in Chu?" },
  { zh: "」曰：「為都尉。", literal: "” He said, “I was commandant.", idiomatic: "” He said, “Commandant." },
  { zh: "」是日，即拜平為都尉，使為參乘，典護軍。", literal: "” That same day Ping was at once appointed commandant, made chariot companion, and put in charge of guarding the army.", idiomatic: "” That same day he was made commandant, chariot companion, and put in charge of the army guard." },
  { zh: "諸將盡讙曰：「大王一日得楚之亡卒，未知其高下，而即與同載，反使監護長者！", literal: "The generals all murmured, saying, “In a single day the Great King got a Chu deserter, does not yet know his worth, yet rides with him at once and instead has him oversee his elders!", idiomatic: "The generals all grumbled: “In one day you took in a Chu runaway whose ability you do not yet know, yet you ride with him and set him to oversee us veterans!" },
  { zh: "」漢王聞之，愈益幸平。", literal: "” When the King of Han heard it, he favored Ping all the more.", idiomatic: "” When the king heard this, he favored Chen Ping all the more." },
  { zh: "13漢王南渡平陰津，至洛陽新城。", literal: "13 The King of Han crossed the Pingyin ford southward and reached Xincheng of Luoyang.", idiomatic: "13 The King of Han crossed the Pingyin ford southward and reached Xincheng near Luoyang." },
  { zh: "三老董公遮說王曰：「臣聞『順德者昌，逆德者亡』；", literal: "the village elder Dong Gong intercepted and urged the king, saying, “Your servant has heard, ‘He who follows virtue flourishes; he who opposes virtue perishes’;", idiomatic: "the village elder Dong Gong stopped the king and said, “I have heard, ‘He who follows virtue flourishes; he who defies virtue perishes’;" },
  { zh: "『兵出無名，事故不成』。", literal: "‘When troops go forth without a righteous name, affairs do not succeed.’", idiomatic: "‘When an army marches without a righteous cause, the enterprise fails.’" },
  { zh: "故曰：『明其為賊，敵乃可服。", literal: "Therefore it is said, ‘Make clear that he is a villain, and the enemy can be subdued.", idiomatic: "Hence the saying, ‘Show him plainly as a villain, and the enemy can be overcome." },
  { zh: "』項羽為無道，放殺其主，天下之賊也。", literal: "’ Xiang Yu is without the Way; he deposed and killed his sovereign—the villain of all under Heaven.", idiomatic: "’ Xiang Yu is lawless; he deposed and killed his sovereign—the villain of the realm." },
  { zh: "夫仁不以勇，義不以力，大王宜率三軍之眾為之素服，以告諸侯而伐之，則四海之內莫不仰德，此三王之舉也。", literal: "Benevolence does not rely on courage, nor righteousness on force; the Great King ought to lead the masses of the three armies in plain mourning garb, announce this to the allies and attack him—then within the four seas none will fail to look up to your virtue. This is the act of the three sage kings.", idiomatic: "Benevolence needs no brute courage, nor righteousness brute force; Your Majesty should lead the army in mourning dress, proclaim this to the allies, and attack him—then all within the seas will look up to your virtue. This is the way of the three sage kings." },
  { zh: "」於是漢王為義帝發喪，袒而大哭，哀臨三日，發使告諸侯曰：「天下共立義帝，北面事之。", literal: "” Thereupon the King of Han held mourning for the Emperor Yi, bared his shoulder and wailed greatly, mourned for three days, and sent envoys to announce to the allies, saying, “All under Heaven jointly established the Emperor Yi and served him facing north.", idiomatic: "” The King of Han then mourned Emperor Yi, bared one shoulder and wailed, observed mourning for three days, and sent envoys to the allies: “All under Heaven jointly set up Emperor Yi and served him as sovereign." },
  { zh: "今項羽放殺義帝江南，大逆無道！", literal: "Now Xiang Yu deposed and killed the Emperor Yi south of the river—great rebellion and absence of the Way!", idiomatic: "Now Xiang Yu deposed and murdered Emperor Yi in the south—great treason and lawlessness!" },
  { zh: "寡人悉發關中兵，收三河士，南浮江、漢以下，願從諸侯王擊楚之殺義帝者！", literal: "I will muster all the troops of Guanzhong, gather the warriors of the Three Rivers, float south down the Yangtze and Han, and wish to follow the allied kings in striking the Chu who killed the Emperor Yi!", idiomatic: "I will muster all Guanzhong's forces, gather the warriors of the Three Rivers, sail south on the Yangtze and Han, and ask the allied kings to join me in punishing Chu for killing Emperor Yi!" },
  { zh: "」使者至趙，陳餘曰：「漢殺張耳，乃從。", literal: "” When the envoy reached Zhao, Chen Yu said, “If Han kills Zhang Er, then I will follow.", idiomatic: "” When the envoy reached Zhao, Chen Yu said, “If Han kills Zhang Er, I will follow." },
  { zh: "」於是漢王求人類張耳者斬之，持其頭遺陳餘；", literal: "” The King of Han then sought a man resembling Zhang Er, beheaded him, and sent his head to Chen Yu;", idiomatic: "” The King of Han found a man who resembled Zhang Er, beheaded him, and sent the head to Chen Yu;" },
  { zh: "餘乃遣兵助漢。", literal: "Yu then sent troops to aid Han.", idiomatic: "Yu then sent troops to help Han." },
  { zh: "14田榮弟橫收散卒，得數萬人，起城陽，夏，四月，立榮子廣為齊王，以拒楚。", literal: "14 Tian Rong's younger brother Heng gathered scattered soldiers, got several tens of thousands of men, rose at Chengyang; in summer, the fourth month, he established Rong's son Guang as King of Qi to resist Chu.", idiomatic: "14 Tian Rong's younger brother Heng gathered scattered troops to several tens of thousands, rose at Chengyang, and in summer, the fourth month, made Rong's son Guang King of Qi to resist Chu." },
  { zh: "項王因留，連戰，未能下。", literal: "The King of Xiang therefore stayed, fought repeatedly, and could not bring them down.", idiomatic: "The King of Xiang therefore remained, fought repeatedly, and could not subdue them." },
  { zh: "雖聞漢東，既擊齊，欲遂破之而後擊漢，漢王以故得率諸侯兵凡五十六萬人伐楚。", literal: "Though he heard Han was moving east, since he was already attacking Qi he wished to break Qi first and then strike Han; for this reason the King of Han was able to lead allied troops totaling five hundred sixty thousand men against Chu.", idiomatic: "Though he heard Han was marching east, he was already attacking Qi and meant to crush Qi before turning on Han; the King of Han therefore led five hundred sixty thousand allied troops against Chu." },
  { zh: "到外黃，彭越將其兵三萬餘人歸漢。", literal: "Reaching Waihuang, Peng Yue led his more than thirty thousand men to rejoin Han.", idiomatic: "At Waihuang, Peng Yue rejoined Han with more than thirty thousand men." },
  { zh: "漢王曰：「彭將軍收魏地得十餘城，欲急立魏後。", literal: "The King of Han said, “General Peng, in recovering Wei territory, has taken more than ten cities and wishes urgently to set up a successor of Wei.", idiomatic: "The King of Han said, “General Peng has recovered more than ten cities in Wei and wishes to set up a successor of Wei at once." },
  { zh: "今西魏王豹，真魏後。", literal: "Now the King of Western Wei, Bao, is the true successor of Wei.", idiomatic: "The King of Western Wei, Bao, is the true heir of Wei." },
  { zh: "」乃拜彭越為魏相國，擅將其兵略定梁地。", literal: "” He then appointed Peng Yue Chancellor of Wei with sole command of his troops to overrun and settle Liang territory.", idiomatic: "” He then made Peng Yue Chancellor of Wei with independent command to secure Liang." },
  { zh: "漢王遂入城，收其貨寶、美人，日置酒高會。", literal: "The King of Han then entered the city, gathered its treasures and beauties, and daily set out wine for grand feasts.", idiomatic: "The King of Han then entered the city, took its treasures and beauties, and daily held grand banquets." },
  { zh: "項王聞之，令諸將擊齊，而自以精兵三萬人南，從魯出胡陵至蕭。", literal: "The King of Xiang heard of it, ordered the generals to attack Qi, and himself with thirty thousand picked troops went south from Lu through Huling to Xiao.", idiomatic: "The King of Xiang heard of it, left his generals to finish Qi, and himself marched south with thirty thousand elite troops from Lu through Huling to Xiao." },
  { zh: "晨，擊漢軍而東至彭城，日中，大破漢軍。", literal: "At dawn he struck the Han army and by midday, having advanced east to Pengcheng, routed the Han army utterly.", idiomatic: "At dawn he struck the Han army; by midday, reaching Pengcheng, he had routed it utterly." },
  { zh: "漢軍皆走，相隨入穀、泗水，死者十餘萬人。", literal: "The Han army all fled, following one another into the Gu and Si rivers; more than a hundred thousand died.", idiomatic: "The Han army fled in masses into the Gu and Si rivers; more than a hundred thousand drowned or were killed." },
  { zh: "漢卒皆南走山，楚又追擊至靈壁東睢水上；", literal: "Han soldiers all fled south into the hills; Chu again pursued to the Sui River east of Lingbi;", idiomatic: "Han troops fled south into the hills; Chu pursued to the Sui River east of Lingbi;" },
  { zh: "漢軍卻，為楚所擠，卒十餘萬人皆入睢水，水為之不流。", literal: "The Han army retreated and was pressed by Chu; more than a hundred thousand soldiers all entered the Sui River, and the water stopped flowing for them.", idiomatic: "The Han army fell back, pressed by Chu; more than a hundred thousand men plunged into the Sui River until the water ceased to flow." },
  { zh: "圍漢王三匝。", literal: "They surrounded the King of Han three deep.", idiomatic: "They surrounded the King of Han in three rings." },
  { zh: "會大風從西北起，折木，發屋，揚沙石，窈冥晝晦，逢迎楚軍，大亂壞散，而漢王乃得與數十騎遁去。", literal: "Just then a great wind rose from the northwest, breaking trees, tearing off roofs, raising sand and stones; darkness made day like night; it met the Chu army head-on; they broke up in great disorder and scattered, and the King of Han was thus able to escape with several dozen horsemen.", idiomatic: "Then a gale rose from the northwest, snapping trees, ripping off roofs, and whipping up sand and stones; day turned dark as night; it struck the Chu army head-on; they broke apart in chaos, and the King of Han escaped with a few dozen riders." },
  { zh: "欲過沛收家室，而楚亦使人之沛取漢王家。", literal: "He wished to pass through Pei to gather his family, but Chu also sent men to Pei to take the King of Han's family.", idiomatic: "He meant to pass through Pei to fetch his household, but Chu also sent men to Pei to seize the King of Han's family." },
  { zh: "家皆亡，不與漢王相見。", literal: "The family had all fled and did not meet the King of Han.", idiomatic: "His household had all fled and never met him." },
  { zh: "漢王道逢孝惠、魯元公主，載以行。", literal: "On the road the King of Han met the Filial and Kind Prince and the Princess of Lu Yuan and carried them along in the carriage.", idiomatic: "On the road the King of Han met the Filial and Kind Prince and the Princess of Lu Yuan and took them into his carriage." },
  { zh: "楚騎追之，漢王急，推墮二子車下。", literal: "Chu horsemen pursued; the King of Han was in urgency and pushed the two children off the carriage.", idiomatic: "Chu cavalry pursued; in his panic the King of Han pushed the two children off the carriage." },
  { zh: "滕公為太僕，常下收載之。", literal: "The Duke of Teng served as grand coachman and regularly got down to pick them up and put them back on the carriage.", idiomatic: "The Duke of Teng, grand coachman, kept leaping down to scoop them up and set them back aboard." },
  { zh: "如是者三，曰：「今雖急，不可以驅，奈何棄之！", literal: "This happened three times; he said, “Though it is urgent now, one cannot drive fast—how can we abandon them!", idiomatic: "This happened three times; he said, “We are in peril, but we cannot drive hard—how can we cast them away!" },
  { zh: "」故徐行。", literal: "” Therefore they went slowly.", idiomatic: "” So they went slowly." },
  { zh: "漢王怒，欲斬之者十餘；", literal: "The King of Han was angry and more than ten times wished to behead him;", idiomatic: "The King of Han was furious and more than ten times meant to behead him;" },
  { zh: "滕公卒保護，脫二子。", literal: "the Duke of Teng in the end protected them and saved the two children.", idiomatic: "the Duke of Teng shielded them to the end and saved both children." },
  { zh: "審食其從太公、呂后間行求漢王，不相遇，反遇楚軍。", literal: "Shen Yishi followed the Grand Duke and Empress Lü by secret route seeking the King of Han; they did not meet him but instead met the Chu army.", idiomatic: "Shen Yishi escorted the Grand Duke and Empress Lü by secret route to find the King of Han; they missed him and ran into the Chu army instead." },
  { zh: "楚軍與歸，項王常置軍中為質。", literal: "Chu took them back; the King of Xiang regularly kept them in the army as hostages.", idiomatic: "Chu took them back; the King of Xiang kept them in camp as hostages." },
  { zh: "是時，呂后兄周呂侯為漢將兵，居下邑。", literal: "At this time the Empress Lü's elder brother the Marquis of Zhou Lü was a Han general with troops stationed at Xiayi.", idiomatic: "At this time the Empress Lü's elder brother, the Marquis of Zhou Lü, commanded Han troops at Xiayi." },
  { zh: "漢王間往從之，稍稍收其士卒。", literal: "The King of Han went by secret route to join him and little by little gathered his soldiers.", idiomatic: "The King of Han slipped away to join him and little by little regathered his troops." },
  { zh: "諸侯皆背漢，復與楚。", literal: "All the allies turned against Han and again sided with Chu.", idiomatic: "The allies all deserted Han and returned to Chu." },
  { zh: "塞王欣、翟王翳亡降楚。", literal: "the King of Sai, Xin, and the King of Di, Yi, fled and surrendered to Chu.", idiomatic: "the Kings of Sai and Di, Sima Xin and Dong Yi, fled and surrendered to Chu." },
  { zh: "15田橫進攻田假，假走楚，楚殺之。", literal: "15 Tian Heng advanced to attack Tian Jia; Jia fled to Chu and Chu killed him.", idiomatic: "15 Tian Heng attacked Tian Jia; Jia fled to Chu, and Chu killed him." },
  { zh: "橫遂復定三齊之地。", literal: "Heng then again settled the territory of the Three Qi.", idiomatic: "Heng then re-established the Three Qi." },
  { zh: "16漢王問群臣曰：「吾欲捐關以東，等棄之，誰可與共功者？", literal: "16 The King of Han asked the ministers, saying, “I wish to give up everything east of the passes and abandon it equally—who can share in the achievement with me?", idiomatic: "16 The King of Han asked his ministers, “I am ready to give up everything east of the passes and share it out—who can work with me to win the realm?" },
  { zh: "」張良曰：「九江王布，楚梟將，與項王有隙；", literal: "” Zhang Liang said, “The King of Jiujiang, Bu, is a Chu bold warrior and has a rift with the King of Xiang;", idiomatic: "” Zhang Liang said, “The King of Jiujiang, Ying Bu, is a formidable Chu commander and is at odds with the King of Xiang;" },
  { zh: "彭越與齊反梁地；", literal: "Peng Yue with Qi is rebelling in Liang territory;", idiomatic: "Peng Yue, with Qi, is stirring rebellion in Liang;" },
  { zh: "此兩人可急使。", literal: "these two men can be urgently deployed.", idiomatic: "these two should be enlisted at once." },
  { zh: "而漢王之將，獨韓信可屬大事，當一面。", literal: "Among the King of Han's generals, only Han Xin can be entrusted with a great matter and hold one front alone.", idiomatic: "Of Your Majesty's generals, only Han Xin can be entrusted with a major command and hold an entire front." },
  { zh: "即欲捐之，捐之此三人，則楚可破也！", literal: "If you wish to give something up, give it up to these three men, and Chu can be broken!", idiomatic: "If you mean to give territory away, give it to these three, and Chu can be broken!" },
  { zh: "初，項王擊齊，徵兵九江，九江王布稱病不在，遣將將軍數千人行。", literal: "At first, when the King of Xiang attacked Qi, he called for troops from Jiujiang; the King of Jiujiang, Bu, claimed illness and did not appear, sending a general with several thousand men.", idiomatic: "Earlier, when the King of Xiang attacked Qi, he called on Jiujiang for troops; the King of Jiujiang, Bu, pleaded illness and stayed away, sending a general with several thousand men." },
  { zh: "漢之破楚彭城，布又稱病不佐楚。", literal: "When Han defeated Chu at Pengcheng, Bu again claimed illness and did not assist Chu.", idiomatic: "When Han routed Chu at Pengcheng, Bu again pleaded illness and refused to aid Chu." },
  { zh: "楚王由此怨布，婁使使者誚讓，召布。", literal: "The King of Chu therefore resented Bu and repeatedly sent envoys to reproach and summon him.", idiomatic: "The King of Chu therefore resented Bu and again and again sent envoys to rebuke and summon him." },
  { zh: "布愈恐，不敢往。", literal: "Bu grew ever more afraid and did not dare go.", idiomatic: "Bu grew more afraid and would not go." },
  { zh: "項王方北憂齊、趙，西患漢，所與者獨九江王；", literal: "The King of Xiang was just then troubled in the north by Qi and Zhao and in the west by Han; the only one allied with him was the King of Jiujiang;", idiomatic: "The King of Xiang was then hard pressed in the north by Qi and Zhao and in the west by Han; his sole ally was the King of Jiujiang;" },
  { zh: "又多布材，欲親用之，以故未之擊。", literal: "he also prized Bu's ability and wished to employ him closely; for this reason he did not attack him.", idiomatic: "he also valued Bu's talent and wished to keep him close; for that reason he did not strike at him." },
  { zh: "漢王自下邑徙軍碭，遂至虞，謂左右曰：「如彼等者，無足與計天下事！", literal: "The King of Han moved his army from Xiayi to Dang, then reached Yu, and said to those about him, “Men like these are not worth consulting on the affairs of all under Heaven!", idiomatic: "The King of Han moved his army from Xiayi to Dang, then reached Yu, and told his attendants, “Men like these are not fit to plan the conquest of the realm!" },
  { zh: "」謁者隨何進曰：「不審陛下所謂。", literal: "” Yeoman Sui He advanced and said, “Your servant does not understand what Your Majesty means.", idiomatic: "” Yeoman Sui He stepped forward and said, “I do not understand what Your Majesty means." },
  { zh: "」漢王曰：「孰能為我使九江，令之發兵倍楚？", literal: "” The King of Han said, “Who can go for me to Jiujiang and make them raise troops and turn against Chu?", idiomatic: "” The King of Han said, “Who can go to Jiujiang for me and make them raise troops and turn on Chu?" },
  { zh: "留項王數月，我之取天下可以百全。", literal: "Hold the King of Xiang for several months, and my taking of all under Heaven can be entirely secure.", idiomatic: "Hold the King of Xiang for several months, and my conquest of the realm will be wholly assured." },
  { zh: "」隨何曰：「臣請使之！", literal: "” Sui He said, “Your servant asks to be sent!", idiomatic: "” Sui He said, “Let me go!" },
  { zh: "」漢王使與二十人俱。", literal: "” The King of Han sent him with twenty men together.", idiomatic: "” The King of Han sent him with twenty companions." },
  { zh: "17五月，漢王至滎陽，諸敗軍皆會，蕭何亦發關中老弱未傅者悉詣滎陽，漢軍復大振。", literal: "17 In the fifth month the King of Han reached Xingyang; all the defeated troops assembled; Xiao He also sent from Guanzhong all the old and weak not yet registered for service to Xingyang; the Han army was again greatly revived.", idiomatic: "17 In the fifth month the King of Han reached Xingyang; the scattered forces rallied; Xiao He also sent every able man in Guanzhong not yet conscripted to Xingyang, and the Han army revived." },
  { zh: "楚起於彭城，常乘勝逐北，與漢戰滎陽南京、索間。", literal: "Chu rose from Pengcheng, constantly pursuing north while victorious, and fought Han between Nanjing of Xingyang and Suo.", idiomatic: "Chu advanced from Pengcheng, always pressing a victorious pursuit northward, and fought Han between the Nanjing and Suo sectors south of Xingyang." },
  { zh: "楚騎來眾，漢王擇軍中可為騎將者，皆推故奉騎士重泉人李必、駱甲。", literal: "Chu cavalry came in great numbers; the King of Han chose from the army who could serve as cavalry generals; all recommended the former Fengxiang cavalrymen Li Bi and Luo Jia of Zhongquan.", idiomatic: "Chu cavalry came in force; the King of Han looked for cavalry commanders, and all named the former Fengxiang horsemen Li Bi and Luo Jia of Zhongquan." },
  { zh: "漢王欲拜之，必、甲曰：「臣故秦民，恐軍不信；", literal: "The King of Han wished to appoint them; Bi and Jia said, “We were formerly subjects of Qin; we fear the army will not trust us;", idiomatic: "The King of Han meant to appoint them; Bi and Jia said, “We are former Qin subjects; the army may not trust us;" },
  { zh: "願得大王左右善騎者傅之。", literal: "we wish to have good horsemen from Your Majesty's attendants to assist us.", idiomatic: "we ask for skilled riders from Your Majesty's staff to assist us." },
  { zh: "」乃拜灌嬰為中大夫令，李必、駱甲為左右校尉，將騎兵擊楚騎於滎陽東，大破之，楚以故不能過滎陽而西。", literal: "” He then appointed Guan Ying lieutenant-commandant director, Li Bi and Luo Jia as left and right commandants, led cavalry to strike Chu cavalry east of Xingyang, routed them utterly; Chu for this reason could not pass west of Xingyang.", idiomatic: "” He appointed Guan Ying director of lieutenant-commandants, Li Bi and Luo Jia as left and right commandants; they led cavalry against Chu east of Xingyang, routed them, and Chu could not break through west of Xingyang." },
  { zh: "漢王軍滎陽，築甬道屬之河，以取敖倉粟。", literal: "The King of Han stationed his army at Xingyang, built a raised corridor connecting to the river, to fetch grain from Aocang.", idiomatic: "The King of Han held Xingyang, built a covered causeway to the river, and drew grain from Aocang." },
  { zh: "18周勃、灌嬰等言於漢王曰：「陳平雖美如冠玉，其中未必有也。", literal: "18 Zhou Bo, Guan Ying, and others spoke to the King of Han, saying, “Though Chen Ping is fair as jade on a cap, inside there may be nothing.", idiomatic: "18 Zhou Bo, Guan Ying, and others told the King of Han, “Chen Ping may look like jade on a cap, but there may be nothing inside." },
  { zh: "臣聞平居家時盜其嫂；", literal: "Your servant hears that when Ping was at home he seduced his sister-in-law;", idiomatic: "We hear that at home he seduced his sister-in-law;" },
  { zh: "事魏不容，亡歸楚；", literal: "serving Wei he was not tolerated and fled to Chu;", idiomatic: "serving Wei he was not kept and fled to Chu;" },
  { zh: "不中，又亡歸漢。", literal: "not succeeding, he fled again to Han.", idiomatic: "failing there, he fled again to Han." },
  { zh: "今日大王尊官之，令護軍。", literal: "Today the Great King honors him with high office and has him guard the army.", idiomatic: "Now Your Majesty honors him and puts him in charge of the army." },
  { zh: "臣聞平受諸將金，金多者得善處，金少者得惡處。", literal: "Your servant hears that Ping receives gold from the generals—those who give much get good assignments, those who give little get bad ones.", idiomatic: "We hear he takes gold from the generals—large gifts win good posts, small gifts win poor ones." },
  { zh: "平，反覆亂臣也，願王察之！", literal: "Ping is a fickle, treacherous minister—may the King examine this!", idiomatic: "Ping is a faithless schemer—may Your Majesty look into it!" },
  { zh: "」漢王疑之，召讓魏無知。", literal: "” The King of Han was suspicious and summoned Wei Wuzhi to reproach him.", idiomatic: "” The King of Han was troubled and summoned Wei Wuzhi to rebuke him." },
  { zh: "無知曰：「臣所言者能也，陛下所問者行也。", literal: "Wuzhi said, “What your servant spoke of was ability; what Your Majesty asks about is conduct.", idiomatic: "Wuzhi said, “I spoke of his ability; Your Majesty asks about his conduct." },
  { zh: "今有尾生、孝己之行，而無益勝負之數，陛下何暇用之乎！", literal: "Now if one had the conduct of Wei Sheng or Xiaoji yet it were of no help to the calculus of victory and defeat, what leisure would Your Majesty have to employ him!", idiomatic: "If a man had the integrity of Wei Sheng or Xiaoji yet it did nothing for victory or defeat, why would Your Majesty bother with him!" },
  { zh: "楚、漢相距，臣進奇謀之士，顧其計誠足以利國家不耳。", literal: "With Chu and Han facing each other, your servant recommends men of strange stratagems—one looks only whether their plans truly suffice to benefit the state or not.", idiomatic: "With Chu and Han locked in struggle, I recommend men of daring stratagem—only whether their plans truly benefit the state matters." },
  { zh: "盜嫂、受金，又何足疑乎！", literal: "Seducing a sister-in-law, accepting gold—what is there worth doubting!", idiomatic: "Seducing a sister-in-law or taking gold—what is there to doubt!" },
  { zh: "」漢王召讓平曰：「先生事魏不中，事楚而去，今又從吾游，信者固多心乎！", literal: "” The King of Han summoned and reproached Ping, saying, “Master, you served Wei without success, served Chu and left; now you follow me—are men of trust naturally full of divided hearts!", idiomatic: "” The King of Han summoned Chen Ping and rebuked him: “You failed in Wei, left Chu, and now follow me—are trustworthy men always so changeable!" },
  { zh: "」平曰：「臣事魏王，魏王不能用臣說，故去；", literal: "” Ping said, “Your servant served the King of Wei; the King of Wei could not use your servant's counsel, so I left;", idiomatic: "” Ping said, “I served the King of Wei; he would not heed me, so I left;" },
  { zh: "事項王，項王不能信人，其所任愛，非諸項，即妻之昆弟，雖有奇士不能用。", literal: "I served the King of Xiang; the King of Xiang cannot trust men—those he employs and favors are none but the various Xiang clansmen or his wife's brothers; though there are extraordinary men he cannot use them.", idiomatic: "I served the King of Xiang; he cannot trust outsiders—those he favors are Xiang clansmen or his wife's kin; even when extraordinary men appear, he will not use them." },
  { zh: "聞漢王能用人，故歸大王。", literal: "I heard the King of Han can employ men, so I came to the Great King.", idiomatic: "I heard that the King of Han knows how to use men, so I came to Your Majesty." },
  { zh: "臣裸身來，不受金無以為資。", literal: "Your servant came naked; without receiving gold there would be no means of support.", idiomatic: "I came with nothing; without gifts I had no means to live." },
  { zh: "誠臣計畫有可采乎，願大王用之；", literal: "If your servant's plans truly have something worth adopting, I wish the Great King to use them;", idiomatic: "If my plans are worth adopting, I beg Your Majesty to use them;" },
  { zh: "使無可用者，金具在，請封輸官，得其骸骨。", literal: "if there are none that can be used, the gold is all still here—please seal it and turn it in to the treasury and grant me my bones to depart.", idiomatic: "if not, the gold is all still here—seal it for the treasury and let me go home to die." },
  { zh: "」漢王乃謝，厚賜，拜為護軍中尉，盡護諸將。", literal: "” The King of Han then apologized, richly rewarded him, appointed him Lieutenant of the Guard for the Army Protectorate, and put all the generals under his guard.", idiomatic: "” The King of Han apologized, richly rewarded him, made him lieutenant of the army protectorate with authority over all the generals." },
  { zh: "諸將乃不敢復言。", literal: "The generals then did not dare speak again.", idiomatic: "The generals then dared say no more." },
  { zh: "19魏王豹謁歸視親疾；", literal: "19 The King of Wei, Bao, asked leave to return and visit his parent in illness;", idiomatic: "19 The King of Wei, Bao, asked leave to go home and tend a parent's illness;" },
  { zh: "至則絕河津，反為楚。", literal: "on arriving he cut off the river crossings and turned to Chu.", idiomatic: "but on arriving he sealed the river crossings and went over to Chu." },
  { zh: "20六月，漢王還櫟陽。", literal: "20 In the sixth month the King of Han returned to Liyang.", idiomatic: "20 In the sixth month the King of Han returned to Liyang." },
  { zh: "21壬午，立子盈為太子；", literal: "21 On renwu day he established his son Ying as crown prince;", idiomatic: "21 On the day renwu he made his son Ying crown prince;" },
  { zh: "赦罪人。", literal: "and pardoned criminals.", idiomatic: "and pardoned criminals." },
  { zh: "22漢兵引水灌廢丘，廢丘降，章邯自殺。", literal: "22 Han troops led water to inundate Feiqiu; Feiqiu surrendered and Zhang Han killed himself.", idiomatic: "22 Han troops diverted water against Feiqiu; Feiqiu surrendered and Zhang Han killed himself." },
  { zh: "盡定雍地，以為中地、北地、隴西郡。", literal: "They entirely settled Yong territory and made it Zhong, Beidi, and Longxi commanderies.", idiomatic: "Yong was wholly pacified and divided into Zhong, Beidi, and Longxi commanderies." },
  { zh: "23關中大饑，米斛萬錢，人相食。", literal: "23 Guanzhong suffered great famine; rice was ten thousand cash per picul and men ate one another.", idiomatic: "23 Guanzhong suffered terrible famine; grain cost ten thousand cash per picul and men ate one another." },
  { zh: "令民就食蜀、漢。", literal: "He ordered the people to go to Shu and Han for food.", idiomatic: "He ordered the people to migrate to Shu and Han for food." },
  { zh: "初，秦之亡也，豪傑爭取金玉，宣曲任氏獨窖倉粟。", literal: "At first when Qin was perishing, the powerful scrambled for gold and jade; the Ren clan of Xuqu alone stored grain in cellars.", idiomatic: "When Qin was collapsing, the powerful scrambled for gold and jade; only the Ren clan of Xuqu hoarded grain in cellars." },
  { zh: "及楚、漢相距滎陽，民不得耕種，而豪傑金玉盡歸任氏，任以此起，富者數世。", literal: "When Chu and Han faced each other at Xingyang the people could not till and plant; the gold and jade of the powerful all went to the Ren clan; the Ren thereby rose and were wealthy for generations.", idiomatic: "When Chu and Han fought at Xingyang and farming ceased, the gold and jade of the powerful all flowed to the Ren clan, who rose on it and stayed rich for generations." },
  { zh: "24秋，八月，漢王如滎陽，命蕭何守關中，侍太子，為法令約束，立宗廟、社稷、宮室、縣邑；", literal: "24 In autumn, the eighth month, the King of Han went to Xingyang and ordered Xiao He to hold Guanzhong, attend the crown prince, set laws and regulations, establish ancestral temples, altars of soil and grain, palaces, counties and towns;", idiomatic: "24 In autumn, the eighth month, the King of Han went to Xingyang and left Xiao He to hold Guanzhong, attend the crown prince, enforce laws, and establish temples, altars, palaces, counties, and towns;" },
  { zh: "事有不及奏決者，輒以便宜施行，上來，以聞。", literal: "matters that could not wait for memorial and decision he might execute on expedient authority; when the sovereign came up he would report.", idiomatic: "what could not wait for the king's decision he might handle on his own authority and report when the king returned." },
  { zh: "計關中戶口，轉漕、調兵以給軍，未嘗乏絕。", literal: "He counted Guanzhong households, transported grain by relay and shifted troops to supply the army—it was never wanting or cut off.", idiomatic: "He tallied Guanzhong households, moved grain and shifted troops to the front, and the army was never left short." },
  { zh: "25漢王使酈食其往說魏王豹，且召之。", literal: "25 The King of Han sent Li Yiji to persuade the King of Wei, Bao, and also to summon him.", idiomatic: "25 The King of Han sent Li Yiji to persuade the King of Wei, Bao, and summon him back." },
  { zh: "豹不聽，曰：「漢王慢而侮人，罵詈諸侯、群臣如罵奴耳，吾不忍復見也。", literal: "Bao would not listen and said, “The King of Han is arrogant and insults men, reviling allies and ministers as one reviles slaves—I cannot bear to see him again.", idiomatic: "Bao refused and said, “The King of Han is arrogant and insulting; he reviles allies and ministers like slaves—I will not see him again." },
  { zh: "」於是漢王以韓信為左丞相，與灌嬰、曹參俱擊魏。", literal: "” Thereupon the King of Han made Han Xin left chancellor and with Guan Ying and Cao Shen together attacked Wei.", idiomatic: "” The King of Han then made Han Xin left chancellor and sent him with Guan Ying and Cao Shen against Wei." },
  { zh: "漢王問食其：「魏大將誰也？", literal: "The King of Han asked Yiji, “Who is Wei's great general?", idiomatic: "The King of Han asked Yiji, “Who is Wei's chief general?" },
  { zh: "」對曰：「柏直。", literal: "” He replied, “Bo Zhi.", idiomatic: "” He answered, “Bo Zhi." },
  { zh: "」王曰：「是口尚乳臭，安能當韓信！", literal: "” The King said, “That mouth still smells of milk—how can he withstand Han Xin!", idiomatic: "” The king said, “He still smells of milk—how can he stand against Han Xin!" },
  { zh: "騎將誰也？", literal: "Who is the cavalry general?", idiomatic: "Who commands the cavalry?" },
  { zh: "」曰：「馮敬。", literal: "” He said, “Feng Jing.", idiomatic: "” He said, “Feng Jing." },
  { zh: "」曰：「是秦將馮無擇子也，雖賢，不能當灌嬰。", literal: "” He said, “He is the son of the Qin general Feng Wuji; though capable, he cannot withstand Guan Ying.", idiomatic: "” He said, “He is the son of the Qin general Feng Wuji; able as he is, he cannot match Guan Ying." },
  { zh: "」「步卒將誰也？", literal: "”“Who is the infantry general?", idiomatic: "”“And who commands the infantry?" },
  { zh: "」曰：「項佗。", literal: "” He said, “Xiang Tuo.", idiomatic: "” He said, “Xiang Tuo." },
  { zh: "」曰：「不能當曹參。", literal: "” He said, “He cannot withstand Cao Shen.", idiomatic: "” He said, “He cannot match Cao Shen." },
  { zh: "吾無患矣！", literal: "I have no worries!", idiomatic: "I have nothing to fear!" },
  { zh: "」韓信亦問酈生：「魏得無用周叔為大將乎？", literal: "” Han Xin also asked Li Yiji, “Would Wei by any chance use Zhou Shu as great general?", idiomatic: "” Han Xin also asked Li Yiji, “Will Wei perhaps use Zhou Shu as chief general?" },
  { zh: "」酈生曰：「柏直也。", literal: "” Yiji said, “Bo Zhi.", idiomatic: "” Yiji said, “Bo Zhi." },
  { zh: "」信曰：「豎子耳。", literal: "” Xin said, “A mere brat.", idiomatic: "” Xin said, “A mere boy." },
  { zh: "」遂進兵。", literal: "” He then advanced the army.", idiomatic: "” He then marched." },
  { zh: "魏王盛兵蒲板以塞臨晉。", literal: "The King of Wei massed troops at Puban to block Linjin.", idiomatic: "The King of Wei massed troops at Puban to block the crossing at Linjin." },
  { zh: "信乃益為疑兵，陳船欲渡臨晉，而伏兵從夏陽以木罌流軍，襲安邑。", literal: "Xin then increased decoy troops, arrayed boats as if to cross at Linjin, while hidden troops from Xiayang floated the army on wooden jars and struck Anyi.", idiomatic: "Xin then staged decoys, lined up boats as if to cross at Linjin, while hidden troops from Xiayang floated the army on wooden jars and struck Anyi." },
  { zh: "魏王豹驚，引兵迎信。", literal: "The King of Wei, Bao, was alarmed and led troops to meet Xin.", idiomatic: "The King of Wei, Bao, was alarmed and marched out to meet Han Xin." },
  { zh: "九月，信擊虜豹，傳詣滎陽；", literal: "In the ninth month Xin struck, captured Bao, and sent him by relay to Xingyang;", idiomatic: "In the ninth month Han Xin attacked, captured Bao, and sent him under escort to Xingyang;" },
  { zh: "悉定魏地，置河東、上黨、太原郡。", literal: "He fully settled Wei territory and established Hedong, Shangdang, and Taiyuan commanderies.", idiomatic: "He fully pacified Wei territory and established Hedong, Shangdang, and Taiyuan commanderies." },
  { zh: "26漢之敗於彭城而西也，陳餘亦覺張耳不死，即背漢。", literal: "26 When Han was defeated at Pengcheng and retreated west, Chen Yu also realized Zhang Er was not dead and at once turned against Han.", idiomatic: "26 When Han was defeated at Pengcheng and retreated west, Chen Yu too realized Zhang Er was alive and at once rebelled against Han." },
  { zh: "韓信既定魏，使人請兵三萬人，願以北舉燕、趙，東擊齊，南絕楚糧道。", literal: "Han Xin, having already settled Wei, sent men to request thirty thousand troops, wishing to raise Yan and Zhao in the north, strike Qi in the east, and cut off Chu's grain routes in the south.", idiomatic: "After Han Xin had pacified Wei, he sent envoys requesting thirty thousand troops, offering to take Yan and Zhao in the north, strike Qi in the east, and cut off Chu's grain routes in the south." },
  { zh: "漢王許之，乃遣張耳與俱，引兵東，北擊趙、代。", literal: "The King of Han agreed and then sent Zhang Er to go with him; he led his troops east and attacked Zhao and Dai in the north.", idiomatic: "The King of Han agreed, sent Zhang Er to accompany him, led his army east, and attacked Zhao and Dai in the north." },
  { zh: "後九月，信破代兵，禽夏說於閼與。", literal: "In the intercalary ninth month Xin defeated the Dai army and captured Xia Yue at Yan Yu.", idiomatic: "In the intercalary ninth month Han Xin routed the Dai army and captured Xia Yue at Yan Yu." },
  { zh: "信之下魏破代，漢輒使人收其精兵詣滎陽以距楚。", literal: "Whenever Xin subdued Wei or defeated Dai, Han would promptly send men to gather his picked troops and bring them to Xingyang to resist Chu.", idiomatic: "Whenever Han Xin took Wei or defeated Dai, the King of Han would promptly send men to gather his elite troops to Xingyang to hold Chu at bay." }
];
